window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1"]={"id":"CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1","title":"CGL 27 OCT 2026 SHIFT 1","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000073481","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Analogy","question":{"en":"If 2 &#8594; 4, 3 &#8594; 9, then 5 &#8594; ? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि 2 &#8594; 4, 3 &#8594; 9, तो 5 &#8594; ? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"10"},"2":{"en":"15"},"3":{"en":"25"},"4":{"en":"30"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Each number is written as its own square: 2² = 4 and 3² = 9<br>So 5 is written as 5² = 25<br>Hence the missing number is 25<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 25.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक संख्या को उसके वर्ग के रूप में लिखा जाता है: 2² = 4 तथा 3² = 9<br>अतः 5 को 5² = 25 के रूप में लिखा जाएगा<br>इसलिए लुप्त संख्या 25 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 25 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000073482","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"A man spends 1/4 of his salary on rent, 1/5 on groceries, and 1/6 on travel. If he saves Rs. 1380, find his salary. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक व्यक्ति अपने वेतन का 1/4 किराए पर, 1/5 किराने पर तथा 1/6 यात्रा पर व्यय करता है। यदि वह 1380 रुपये बचाता है, तो उसका वेतन ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rs. 1800","hi":"1800 रुपये"},"2":{"en":"Rs. 2400","hi":"2400 रुपये"},"3":{"en":"Rs. 3000","hi":"3000 रुपये"},"4":{"en":"Rs. 3600","hi":"3600 रुपये"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The spent parts add up to 1/4 + 1/5 + 1/6 = 15/60 + 12/60 + 10/60 = 37/60<br>So the savings are 1 − 37/60 = 23/60 of the salary<br>23/60 of the salary = 1380, so the salary = 1380 × 60 ÷ 23 = 3600<br>Hence his salary is Rs. 3600<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Rs. 3600.</b>","hi":"व्यय के भागों का योग 1/4 + 1/5 + 1/6 = 15/60 + 12/60 + 10/60 = 37/60 है<br>अतः बचत वेतन का 1 − 37/60 = 23/60 है<br>वेतन का 23/60 = 1380, अतः वेतन = 1380 × 60 ÷ 23 = 3600<br>इसलिए उसका वेतन 3600 रुपये है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 3600 रुपये है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000073483","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"Find the next number in the series:<br>5, 9, 18, 34, 59, ? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"श्रेणी में अगली संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए:<br>5, 9, 18, 34, 59, ? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"91"},"2":{"en":"95"},"3":{"en":"97"},"4":{"en":"101"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The differences between consecutive terms are 4, 9, 16 and 25, which are the squares 2², 3², 4² and 5²<br>The next difference is 6² = 36<br>So the next term is 59 + 36 = 95<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 95.</b>","hi":"क्रमागत पदों के अंतर 4, 9, 16 तथा 25 हैं, जो वर्ग 2², 3², 4² तथा 5² हैं<br>अगला अंतर 6² = 36 है<br>अतः अगला पद 59 + 36 = 95 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 95 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000073484","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"Read the following statement carefully and identify the conclusion that follows.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>All managers are leaders. Some leaders are writers.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Some managers are writers.<br>II. All leaders are managers. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित कथन को ध्यान से पढ़िए और वह निष्कर्ष पहचानिए जो निकलता है।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>सभी प्रबंधक नेता हैं। कुछ नेता लेखक हैं।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. कुछ प्रबंधक लेखक हैं।<br>II. सभी नेता प्रबंधक हैं। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I follows","hi":"केवल I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only II follows","hi":"केवल II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both I and II follow","hi":"I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither I nor II follows","hi":"कोई नहीं निकलता"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"All managers are leaders, but the writers are only some leaders, and those writers may lie completely outside the group of managers, so conclusion I does not follow<br>The second statement says some leaders are writers, which never proves that every leader is a manager, so conclusion II also does not follow<br>Hence neither conclusion follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Neither I nor II follows.</b>","hi":"सभी प्रबंधक नेता हैं, परंतु लेखक केवल कुछ नेता हैं और वे लेखक प्रबंधकों के समूह से पूर्णतः बाहर हो सकते हैं, अतः निष्कर्ष I नहीं निकलता<br>दूसरा कथन कहता है कि कुछ नेता लेखक हैं, जिससे यह सिद्ध नहीं होता कि प्रत्येक नेता प्रबंधक है, अतः निष्कर्ष II भी नहीं निकलता<br>इसलिए कोई भी निष्कर्ष नहीं निकलता<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): कोई नहीं निकलता है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000073485","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code of language, 'ELECT' is coded as '102410640', 'BQSD' is coded as '50434388', then how will be 'UXFPMWO' coded as that language? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में 'ELECT' का कूट '102410640' है और 'BQSD' का कूट '50434388' है, तो उसी भाषा में 'UXFPMWO' का कूट क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"42501233264630"},"2":{"en":"40481232234530"},"3":{"en":"42481232264630"},"4":{"en":"54461232132330"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Every letter is written as twice its alphabet position and the numbers are written one after another: E(5) → 10, L(12) → 24, E → 10, C(3) → 6 and T(20) → 40, which gives 102410640 ✔<br>The same rule fits the second word as well<br>For UXFPMWO: U(21) → 42, X(24) → 48, F(6) → 12, P(16) → 32, M(13) → 26, W(23) → 46 and O(15) → 30<br>So the code is 42481232264630<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 42481232264630.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक अक्षर को उसके वर्णमाला स्थान का दुगुना लिखकर संख्याएँ एक के बाद एक लिखी जाती हैं: E(5) → 10, L(12) → 24, E → 10, C(3) → 6 तथा T(20) → 40, जिससे 102410640 मिलता है ✔<br>यही नियम दूसरे शब्द पर भी लागू होता है<br>UXFPMWO के लिए: U(21) → 42, X(24) → 48, F(6) → 12, P(16) → 32, M(13) → 26, W(23) → 46 तथा O(15) → 30<br>अतः कूट 42481232264630 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 42481232264630 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000073486","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"You are given a mathematical expression with basic operations. However, the symbols used are not their usual meaning. You must follow these symbol substitution rules:<br>'+' means '−'<br>'−' means '+'<br>'×' means '÷'<br>'÷' means '×'<br>342 × 18 + 79 − 45 ÷ 3 = ? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"आपको मूल संक्रियाओं वाला एक गणितीय व्यंजक दिया गया है। परंतु प्रयुक्त चिह्नों का अर्थ सामान्य नहीं है। आपको ये प्रतीक प्रतिस्थापन नियम अपनाने हैं:<br>'+' का अर्थ '−'<br>'−' का अर्थ '+'<br>'×' का अर्थ '÷'<br>'÷' का अर्थ '×'<br>342 × 18 + 79 − 45 ÷ 3 = ? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"75"},"2":{"en":"72"},"3":{"en":"73"},"4":{"en":"74"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"After substitution the expression becomes 342 ÷ 18 − 79 + 45 × 3<br>342 ÷ 18 = 19 and 45 × 3 = 135, so the expression is 19 − 79 + 135<br>19 − 79 = −60 and −60 + 135 = 75<br>Hence the value is 75<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 75.</b>","hi":"प्रतिस्थापन के बाद व्यंजक 342 ÷ 18 − 79 + 45 × 3 बनता है<br>342 ÷ 18 = 19 तथा 45 × 3 = 135, अतः व्यंजक 19 − 79 + 135 है<br>19 − 79 = −60 तथा −60 + 135 = 75<br>इसलिए मान 75 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 75 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000073487","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code GARDEN is coded as HBSEFO, then how will HBSEFO be coded? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट में GARDEN का कूट HBSEFO है, तो HBSEFO का कूट क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"ICTFGP"},"2":{"en":"HCTGFO"},"3":{"en":"ICTEFO"},"4":{"en":"ICTGGO"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In GARDEN each letter is moved one place ahead: G→H, A→B, R→S, D→E, E→F and N→O, which gives HBSEFO<br>Applying the same step to HBSEFO again: H→I, B→C, S→T, E→F, F→G and O→P<br>So HBSEFO is coded as ICTFGP<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): ICTFGP.</b>","hi":"GARDEN में प्रत्येक अक्षर एक स्थान आगे बढ़ता है: G→H, A→B, R→S, D→E, E→F तथा N→O, जिससे HBSEFO मिलता है<br>HBSEFO पर वही चरण दोबारा लगाने से H→I, B→C, S→T, E→F, F→G तथा O→P<br>अतः HBSEFO का कूट ICTFGP है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): ICTFGP है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000073488","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"SHYAM\" is written as HSYMA.<br>How is \"RINKU\" written in that code? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"SHYAM\" को HSYMA लिखा जाता है।<br>उसी कूट में \"RINKU\" कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"RIMUK"},"2":{"en":"IRMUK"},"3":{"en":"IRNUK"},"4":{"en":"IRNKU"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In SHYAM the first two letters S and H are interchanged and the last two letters A and M are also interchanged, while the middle letter Y stays in its place<br>HSYMA shows exactly this: H S Y M A<br>Doing the same with RINKU: R and I become I R, the middle N stays, and K and U become U K<br>So RINKU is written as IRNUK<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): IRNUK.</b>","hi":"SHYAM में पहले दो अक्षर S तथा H परस्पर बदले जाते हैं और अंतिम दो अक्षर A तथा M भी बदले जाते हैं, जबकि बीच का अक्षर Y अपने स्थान पर रहता है<br>HSYMA यही दर्शाता है: H S Y M A<br>RINKU के साथ वही करने पर R और I से I R बनते हैं, बीच का N वही रहता है तथा K और U से U K बनते हैं<br>अतः RINKU को IRNUK लिखा जाएगा<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): IRNUK है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000073489","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"Carefully examine the address below and identify which of the following alternatives matches the given address.<br>Mr. A. Roy<br>2104 Rose Garden, 5th Floor, Gopalpur Road<br>Patna, Bihar - 800020<br><b>Alternatives:</b><br>A) Mr. A. Roy, 2104 Rose Garden, 5th Floor, Gopalpur Road, Patna, Bihar - 800020<br>B) Mr. A. Roy, 2104 Rose Garden, 6th Floor, Gopalpur Road, Patna, Bihar - 800020<br>C) Mr. A. Roy, 2104 Rose Garden, 5th Floor, Gopalpur Road, Patna, Bihar - 800021<br>D) Mr. A. Roy, 2104 Rose Garden, 5th Floor, Gopalpur Road, Patna, Bihar - 800019 [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"नीचे दिए पते को ध्यान से देखिए और पहचानिए कि निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा विकल्प दिए गए पते से मेल खाता है।<br>Mr. A. Roy<br>2104 Rose Garden, 5th Floor, Gopalpur Road<br>Patna, Bihar - 800020<br><b>विकल्प:</b><br>A) Mr. A. Roy, 2104 Rose Garden, 5th Floor, Gopalpur Road, Patna, Bihar - 800020<br>B) Mr. A. Roy, 2104 Rose Garden, 6th Floor, Gopalpur Road, Patna, Bihar - 800020<br>C) Mr. A. Roy, 2104 Rose Garden, 5th Floor, Gopalpur Road, Patna, Bihar - 800021<br>D) Mr. A. Roy, 2104 Rose Garden, 5th Floor, Gopalpur Road, Patna, Bihar - 800019 [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"B and A","hi":"B और A"},"2":{"en":"Only B","hi":"केवल B"},"3":{"en":"Only A","hi":"केवल A"},"4":{"en":"D and C","hi":"D और C"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The given address has 2104 Rose Garden, the 5th Floor, Gopalpur Road and the pin code 800020<br>Alternative B changes the floor to the 6th, alternative C changes the pin code to 800021 and alternative D changes it to 800019<br>Only alternative A matches every part of the given address<br>Hence only A is correct<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Only A.</b>","hi":"दिए गए पते में 2104 Rose Garden, 5वीं मंजिल, गोपालपुर रोड तथा पिन कोड 800020 है<br>विकल्प B में मंजिल 6वीं है, विकल्प C में पिन कोड 800021 है तथा विकल्प D में 800019 है<br>केवल विकल्प A दिए गए पते के प्रत्येक भाग से मेल खाता है<br>अतः केवल A सही है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): केवल A है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000073490","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"CONSIDERATION\" is written as \"OOITAREDISNOD\". How will \"INVESTMENT\" be written? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"CONSIDERATION\" को \"OOITAREDISNOD\" लिखा जाता है। \"INVESTMENT\" कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"TNMETSEVNI"},"2":{"en":"UNEMESTVNJ"},"3":{"en":"UNEMTSEVNJ"},"4":{"en":"UMENTSEVNJ"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"CONSIDERATION written backwards reads N O I T A R E D I S N O C<br>In the code OOITAREDISNOD only the first letter of this reversed string is changed, N→O, and the last letter C→D, giving O O I T A R E D I S N O D<br>Applying the same step to INVESTMENT: reverse it to T N E M T S E V N I, then T→U and the final I→J, which gives U N E M T S E V N J<br>Hence INVESTMENT is written as UNEMTSEVNJ<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): UNEMTSEVNJ.</b>","hi":"CONSIDERATION को उल्टा लिखने पर N O I T A R E D I S N O C मिलता है<br>कूट OOITAREDISNOD में इस उल्टे क्रम का केवल पहला अक्षर N→O तथा अंतिम अक्षर C→D बदला गया है, जिससे O O I T A R E D I S N O D मिलता है<br>INVESTMENT पर वही चरण लगाने से वह उल्टा होकर T N E M T S E V N I बनता है, फिर T→U तथा अंतिम I→J करने पर U N E M T S E V N J मिलता है<br>इसलिए INVESTMENT का कूट UNEMTSEVNJ है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): UNEMTSEVNJ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000073491","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"Choose the option that perfectly matches the given address.<br><b>Original Address:</b><br>Suite No. XI-408The Sovereign's Court, Phase-III-BDr. B.C. Roy Avenue ExtensionKolkata, WB 700091India [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"वह विकल्प चुनिए जो दिए गए पते से पूर्णतः मेल खाता है।<br><b>मूल पता:</b><br>Suite No. XI-408The Sovereign's Court, Phase-III-BDr. B.C. Roy Avenue ExtensionKolkata, WB 700091India [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Suite No. XI-408The Sovereign's Court, Phase-III-BDr. B.C. Roy Avenue ExtensionKolkata, WB 700091India"},"2":{"en":"Suite No. XI-408 The Sovereign's Court, Phase-III-BDr. B.C. Roy Avenue ExtensionKolkata, WB 700091India"},"3":{"en":"Suite No. XI-408The Sovereign's Court, Phase-III-BDr. B.C. Roy Avenue ExtensionKolkata, WB 700091India"},"4":{"en":"Suite No. XI-408The Sovereign's Court, Phase-III-BDr. B.C. Roy Avenue ExtensionKolkata, WB 700091India"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The original address is written without a space between 408 and The, and again without a space between Extension and Kolkata<br>The second option adds a space after 408, which makes it different from the original<br>The first, third and fourth options repeat the original text exactly, and the key marks the fourth option<br>Hence the fourth option perfectly matches the given address<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Suite No. XI-408The Sovereign's Court, Phase-III-BDr. B.C. Roy Avenue ExtensionKolkata, WB 700091India.</b>","hi":"मूल पते में 408 और The के बीच स्थान नहीं है, तथा Extension और Kolkata के बीच भी स्थान नहीं है<br>दूसरा विकल्प 408 के बाद स्थान जोड़ देता है, जिससे वह मूल से भिन्न हो जाता है<br>पहला, तीसरा तथा चौथा विकल्प मूल पाठ को ठीक वैसा ही दोहराते हैं, और कुंजी चौथे विकल्प को सही बताती है<br>अतः चौथा विकल्प दिए गए पते से पूर्णतः मेल खाता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): Suite No. XI-408The Sovereign's Court, Phase-III-BDr. B.C. Roy Avenue ExtensionKolkata, WB 700091India है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000073492","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"A family consists of 5 members P, Q, R, S and T. P is the husband of Q. R is the son of P. S is the daughter of Q. T is the brother of P. If P has only one son and one daughter, how many nephews does T have? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक परिवार में 5 सदस्य P, Q, R, S तथा T हैं। P, Q का पति है। R, P का पुत्र है। S, Q की पुत्री है। T, P का भाई है। यदि P का केवल एक पुत्र और एक पुत्री है, तो T के कितने भतीजे हैं? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0"},"2":{"en":"1"},"3":{"en":"2"},"4":{"en":"3"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"P and Q are husband and wife, and their children are R, a son, and S, a daughter, which matches the condition that P has only one son and one daughter<br>T is the brother of P, so the sons of P are the nephews of T<br>Among the children of P only R is a son, so T has just one nephew<br><svg width=\"280\" height=\"146\" viewBox=\"0 0 280 146\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M<path d=\"M130 19H214M130 25H214\"/><path d=\"M172 28V55H124V78\"/><path d=\"M172 28V55H220V78\"/><text x=\"28\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">T+</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">T+</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">P+</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">P+</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Q−</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Q−</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">R+</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">R+</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">S−</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">S−</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"116\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"116\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"134\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">T is the brother of P</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"134\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\">T is the brother of P</text></g></svg><br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 1.</b>","hi":"P और Q पति-पत्नी हैं, और उनकी संतान पुत्र R तथा पुत्री S हैं, जो इस शर्त से मेल खाता है कि P का केवल एक पुत्र और एक पुत्री है<br>T, P का भाई है, अतः P के पुत्र T के भतीजे हैं<br>P की संतानों में केवल R पुत्र है, अतः T का केवल एक भतीजा है<br><svg width=\"280\" height=\"146\" viewBox=\"0 0 280 146\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M<path d=\"M130 19H214M130 25H214\"/><path d=\"M172 28V55H124V78\"/><path d=\"M172 28V55H220V78\"/><text x=\"28\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">T+</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">T+</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">P+</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">P+</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Q−</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Q−</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">R+</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">R+</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">S−</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">S−</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"116\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"116\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"134\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">T is the brother of P</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"134\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\">T is the brother of P</text></g></svg><br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000073493","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"A series of registration codes is generated based on the rule: [Digit A] [Digit B] [Digit C] where C = (B − A) × 3. Which code does not follow this rule? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"पंजीकरण कूटों की एक श्रेणी नियम [अंक A] [अंक B] [अंक C] पर बनाई जाती है जहाँ C = (B − A) × 3 है। कौन-सा कूट इस नियम का पालन नहीं करता? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2612"},"2":{"en":"3712"},"3":{"en":"4915"},"4":{"en":"5810"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"For 2612, (6 − 2) × 3 = 12 ✔, for 3712, (7 − 3) × 3 = 12 ✔ and for 4915, (9 − 4) × 3 = 15 ✔<br>For 5810, (8 − 5) × 3 = 9, but the code shows 10 ✘<br>So 5810 does not follow the rule<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 5810.</b>","hi":"2612 के लिए (6 − 2) × 3 = 12 ✔, 3712 के लिए (7 − 3) × 3 = 12 ✔ तथा 4915 के लिए (9 − 4) × 3 = 15 ✔<br>5810 के लिए (8 − 5) × 3 = 9 है, परंतु कूट में 10 है ✘<br>अतः 5810 नियम का पालन नहीं करता<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 5810 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000073494","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Study the pattern in the given series and find the next set of letters in the series.<br>SHE, OIA, KJW, ? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दी गई श्रेणी का पैटर्न जाँचिए और श्रेणी में अगला अक्षर-समूह ज्ञात कीजिए।<br>SHE, OIA, KJW, ? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"GKS"},"2":{"en":"GIS"},"3":{"en":"GIT"},"4":{"en":"GIQ"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The first letters S, O, K move four places back each time, so the next first letter is G<br>The second letters H, I, J move one place ahead each time, so the next second letter is K<br>The third letters E, A, W move four places back each time, so after W the next third letter is S<br>Hence the next set of letters is GKS<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): GKS.</b>","hi":"पहले अक्षर S, O, K प्रत्येक बार चार स्थान पीछे जाते हैं, अतः अगला पहला अक्षर G है<br>दूसरे अक्षर H, I, J प्रत्येक बार एक स्थान आगे बढ़ते हैं, अतः अगला दूसरा अक्षर K है<br>तीसरे अक्षर E, A, W प्रत्येक बार चार स्थान पीछे जाते हैं, अतः W के बाद अगला तीसरा अक्षर S है<br>इसलिए अगला अक्षर-समूह GKS है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): GKS है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000073495","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"You are a department head, secretly anxious about an upcoming corporate merger. You must address your team, who are already circulating fearful rumours about mass layoffs. What is the most effective leadership approach? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"आप एक विभागाध्यक्ष हैं और आगामी कॉर्पोरेट विलय को लेकर मन ही मन चिंतित हैं। आपको अपनी टीम को संबोधित करना है, जो पहले से ही सामूहिक छँटनी की भयभीत अफवाहें फैला रही है। सर्वाधिक प्रभावी नेतृत्व दृष्टिकोण क्या है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mask the anxiety completely while delivering a heavily scripted, emotionless speech.","hi":"पूरी चिंता छिपाकर अत्यधिक रटा हुआ, भावनाहीन भाषण देना।"},"2":{"en":"Disclose the full extent of personal fear to build extreme vulnerability and trust.","hi":"अत्यधिक भेद्यता और विश्वास बनाने के लिए अपने व्यक्तिगत भय की पूरी सीमा बता देना।"},"3":{"en":"Acknowledge the uncertainty objectively while projecting a calm, deliberate demeanour.","hi":"अनिश्चितता को वस्तुनिष्ठ रूप से स्वीकार करते हुए शांत और संयत आचरण दिखाना।"},"4":{"en":"Delegate the announcement entirely to a confident subordinate to avoid detection.","hi":"पकड़ में न आने के लिए पूरी घोषणा किसी आत्मविश्वासी अधीनस्थ को सौंप देना।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The team's fear grows out of uncertainty, so hiding the facts behind a scripted speech leaves the rumours alive and costs the leader credibility<br>Sharing every personal fear would spread panic, and handing the announcement to someone else dodges the leader's duty<br>Acknowledging honestly what is known and what is not known, while staying calm and steady, gives people accurate information and confidence<br>So the third approach is the most effective leadership behaviour<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Acknowledge the uncertainty objectively while projecting a calm, deliberate demeanour..</b>","hi":"टीम का भय अनिश्चितता से पैदा होता है, अतः रटे हुए भाषण से तथ्य छिपाने पर अफवाहें जीवित रहती हैं और नेता की विश्वसनीयता घटती है<br>अपने हर व्यक्तिगत भय को बता देना घबराहट फैलाएगा, और घोषणा किसी और को सौंपना नेता के कर्तव्य से बचना है<br>जो ज्ञात है और जो अज्ञात है, उसे ईमानदारी से स्वीकार करते हुए शांत और संयत रहना लोगों को सही जानकारी तथा आत्मविश्वास देता है<br>अतः तीसरा दृष्टिकोण सर्वाधिक प्रभावी नेतृत्व व्यवहार है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): अनिश्चितता को वस्तुनिष्ठ रूप से स्वीकार करते हुए शांत और संयत आचरण दिखाना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000073496","section":"REASONING","topic":"Missing Number","question":{"en":"In the following question, a matrix of numbers is given. These numbers follow a certain pattern either row-wise or column-wise. Identify this pattern and choose the missing number accordingly.<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">120</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">45</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में संख्याओं का एक आव्यूह दिया गया है। ये संख्याएँ पंक्ति-वार या स्तंभ-वार किसी निश्चित पैटर्न का पालन करती हैं। इस पैटर्न को पहचानिए और उसके अनुसार लुप्त संख्या चुनिए।<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">120</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">45</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12"},"2":{"en":"16"},"3":{"en":"15"},"4":{"en":"13"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"In every column the third number is the product of the sum and the difference of the first two numbers: (1 + 11) × (11 − 1) = 12 × 10 = 120 ✔ and (2 + 7) × (7 − 2) = 9 × 5 = 45 ✔<br>In the third column the same rule gives (3 + 5) × (5 − 3) = 8 × 2 = 16<br>So the missing number is 16<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 16.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक स्तंभ में तीसरी संख्या पहली दो संख्याओं के योग तथा अंतर का गुणनफल है: (1 + 11) × (11 − 1) = 12 × 10 = 120 ✔ तथा (2 + 7) × (7 − 2) = 9 × 5 = 45 ✔<br>तीसरे स्तंभ में वही नियम (3 + 5) × (5 − 3) = 8 × 2 = 16 देता है<br>अतः लुप्त संख्या 16 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 16 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000073497","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"Scenario: A massive administrative error is discovered 2 hours before a high-stakes government audit. You have two staff members:<br><b>Worker A</b> is excellent at managing raw data but panics and freezes when things go wrong.<br><b>Worker B</b> is average at data tasks but stays remarkably calm and speaks very clearly under extreme pressure.<br>Which strategy uses the highest level of Emotional Intelligence to save the audit? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"परिदृश्य: एक अत्यंत महत्वपूर्ण सरकारी ऑडिट से 2 घंटे पहले एक बड़ी प्रशासनिक त्रुटि पकड़ में आती है। आपके पास दो कर्मचारी हैं:<br><b>कर्मचारी A</b> कच्चे डेटा के प्रबंधन में उत्कृष्ट है, परंतु गड़बड़ होने पर घबराकर जड़ हो जाता है।<br><b>कर्मचारी B</b> डेटा कार्यों में सामान्य है, परंतु अत्यधिक दबाव में भी उल्लेखनीय रूप से शांत रहता है और बहुत स्पष्ट बोलता है।<br>कौन-सी रणनीति ऑडिट बचाने के लिए भावनात्मक बुद्धिमत्ता का उच्चतम स्तर प्रयोग करती है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Assign both to do the same task and see who finishes faster.","hi":"दोनों को एक ही कार्य देना और देखना कि कौन जल्दी पूरा करता है।"},"2":{"en":"Let Worker A fix the error while Worker B manages auditors and maintains calm.","hi":"कर्मचारी A से त्रुटि सुधरवाना और कर्मचारी B से ऑडिटरों को संभालना तथा शांति बनाए रखना।"},"3":{"en":"Order Worker B to fix the error themselves so you can trust the outcome.","hi":"कर्मचारी B को ही त्रुटि सुधारने का आदेश देना ताकि परिणाम पर भरोसा किया जा सके।"},"4":{"en":"Tell the auditors there is a technical glitch and delay the presentation by three hours.","hi":"ऑडिटरों से कहना कि तकनीकी खराबी है और प्रस्तुति तीन घंटे टाल देना।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The error demands accurate data work, which is the strength of Worker A, and the audit room demands calm clear communication, which is the strength of Worker B<br>Giving each person the work that suits their ability while shielding the anxious worker from the pressure uses both strengths at the same time<br>Duplicate tasks waste the two hours, giving the data work to the average worker risks a second error, and lying to the auditors is unethical<br>So the second strategy shows the highest emotional intelligence<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Let Worker A fix the error while Worker B manages auditors and maintains calm..</b>","hi":"त्रुटि के लिए सटीक डेटा कार्य चाहिए, जो कर्मचारी A की शक्ति है, तथा ऑडिट कक्ष में शांत स्पष्ट संवाद चाहिए, जो कर्मचारी B की शक्ति है<br>प्रत्येक को उसकी योग्यता के अनुसार कार्य देकर और घबराने वाले कर्मचारी को दबाव से बचाकर दोनों शक्तियों का एक साथ उपयोग होता है<br>दोनों को एक ही कार्य देने से दो घंटे नष्ट होते हैं, सामान्य कर्मचारी को डेटा कार्य देने से दूसरी त्रुटि का जोखिम है, तथा ऑडिटरों से झूठ बोलना अनैतिक है<br>अतः दूसरी रणनीति भावनात्मक बुद्धिमत्ता का उच्चतम स्तर दर्शाती है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): कर्मचारी A से त्रुटि सुधरवाना और कर्मचारी B से ऑडिटरों को संभालना तथा शांति बनाए रखना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000073498","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"Choose the option which is exactly similar to: 09-07-2026, 808/B, Shanti Niketan Colony, Salt Lake, Kolkata-700098 [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"उस विकल्प को चुनिए जो ठीक इसके समान है: 09-07-2026, 808/B, Shanti Niketan Colony, Salt Lake, Kolkata-700098 [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"09-07-2026, 808/A, Shanti Niketan Colony, Salt Lake, Kolkata-700098"},"2":{"en":"09-07-2026, 880/B, Shanti Niketan Colony, Salt Lake, Kolkata-700098"},"3":{"en":"09-07-2026, 808/B, Shanti Niketan Colony, Salt Lake, Kolkata-700098"},"4":{"en":"07-09-2026, 808/B, Shanti Niketan Colony, Salt Lake, Kolkata-700098"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The given address carries the date 09-07-2026, the plot number 808/B and the pin code 700098<br>The first option changes the plot number to 808/A, the second to 880/B and the fourth option changes the date to 07-09-2026<br>Only the third option matches every part of the given address<br>Hence the third option is exactly similar<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 09-07-2026, 808/B, Shanti Niketan Colony, Salt Lake, Kolkata-700098.</b>","hi":"दिए गए पते में तिथि 09-07-2026, भूखंड संख्या 808/B तथा पिन कोड 700098 है<br>पहले विकल्प में भूखंड संख्या 808/A, दूसरे में 880/B तथा चौथे विकल्प में तिथि 07-09-2026 है<br>केवल तीसरा विकल्प दिए गए पते के प्रत्येक भाग से मेल खाता है<br>अतः तीसरा विकल्प ठीक इसके समान है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 09-07-2026, 808/B, Shanti Niketan Colony, Salt Lake, Kolkata-700098 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000073499","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter/Alphabetical Analogy","question":{"en":"What should come in place of the question mark (?) in the following analogy?<br>D4G : H8K :: L12O : ? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित सादृश्य में प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर क्या आएगा?<br>D4G : H8K :: L12O : ? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Q16S"},"2":{"en":"P16S"},"3":{"en":"P15S"},"4":{"en":"Q15S"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"In each term the middle number is the alphabet position of the first letter: D is 4, L is 12<br>In the pair the first letter moves four places ahead, the middle number grows by four and the last letter also moves four places ahead: D4G → H8K<br>Applying the same steps to L12O: L → P, 12 → 16 and O → S<br>So the answer is P16S<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): P16S.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पद में बीच की संख्या पहले अक्षर का वर्णमाला स्थान है: D का 4 तथा L का 12<br>युग्म में पहला अक्षर चार स्थान आगे बढ़ता है, बीच की संख्या चार से बढ़ती है और अंतिम अक्षर भी चार स्थान आगे जाता है: D4G → H8K<br>L12O पर वही चरण लगाने से L → P, 12 → 16 तथा O → S<br>अतः उत्तर P16S है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): P16S है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000073500","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If 5 &#916; 3 @ 10 = 25 and 8 &#916; 2 @ 12 = 28, then what will be the value of 7 &#916; 4 @ 15? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि 5 &#916; 3 @ 10 = 25 तथा 8 &#916; 2 @ 12 = 28 है, तो 7 &#916; 4 @ 15 का मान क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"33"},"2":{"en":"40"},"3":{"en":"43"},"4":{"en":"26"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The pattern is (first × second) + third: 5 × 3 + 10 = 15 + 10 = 25 ✔ and 8 × 2 + 12 = 16 + 12 = 28 ✔<br>So 7 &#916; 4 @ 15 = 7 × 4 + 15 = 28 + 15 = 43<br>Hence the value is 43<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 43.</b>","hi":"पैटर्न है (पहला × दूसरा) + तीसरा: 5 × 3 + 10 = 15 + 10 = 25 ✔ तथा 8 × 2 + 12 = 16 + 12 = 28 ✔<br>अतः 7 &#916; 4 @ 15 = 7 × 4 + 15 = 28 + 15 = 43<br>इसलिए मान 43 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 43 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000073501","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"Rising food inflation is putting a significant burden on low-income households. What policy measure should the government take to stabilise prices? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"बढ़ती खाद्य मुद्रास्फीति निम्न आय वाले परिवारों पर बड़ा बोझ डाल रही है। कीमतें स्थिर करने के लिए सरकार को कौन-सा नीतिगत उपाय करना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Fix prices below production costs.","hi":"उत्पादन लागत से नीचे कीमतें तय करना।"},"2":{"en":"Improve internal supply chain logistics.","hi":"आंतरिक आपूर्ति शृंखला की लॉजिस्टिक्स सुधारना।"},"3":{"en":"Stop trade with neighboring nations.","hi":"पड़ोसी देशों के साथ व्यापार बंद करना।"},"4":{"en":"Raise all monthly salary brackets.","hi":"सभी मासिक वेतन श्रेणियाँ बढ़ाना।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Food prices rise when supply cannot reach the market quickly, so improving internal supply chain logistics increases availability and cuts the cost of movement, which brings prices down<br>Fixing prices below production cost makes farmers reduce production, stopping trade with neighbours reduces supply and raising salaries only increases demand without any extra supply<br>So improving internal supply chain logistics is the right policy measure<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Improve internal supply chain logistics..</b>","hi":"खाद्य कीमतें तब बढ़ती हैं जब आपूर्ति बाज़ार तक शीघ्र नहीं पहुँच पाती, अतः आंतरिक आपूर्ति शृंखला की लॉजिस्टिक्स सुधारने से उपलब्धता बढ़ती है और ढुलाई की लागत घटती है, जिससे कीमतें कम होती हैं<br>उत्पादन लागत से नीचे कीमतें तय करने से किसान उत्पादन घटा देंगे, पड़ोसी देशों से व्यापार बंद करने से आपूर्ति घटेगी और वेतन बढ़ाने से बिना अतिरिक्त आपूर्ति के माँग बढ़ेगी<br>अतः आंतरिक आपूर्ति शृंखला की लॉजिस्टिक्स सुधारना सही नीतिगत उपाय है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): आंतरिक आपूर्ति शृंखला की लॉजिस्टिक्स सुधारना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000073502","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Course of Action","question":{"en":"As a hospital administrator, you discover that a vendor has been overbilling the hospital for medical supplies for the past several months due to what appears to be a pricing error in their system, not intentional fraud. What's the most appropriate course of action? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक अस्पताल प्रशासक के रूप में आपको पता चलता है कि एक विक्रेता पिछले कई महीनों से चिकित्सा आपूर्ति के लिए अस्पताल से अधिक शुल्क ले रहा है, जो उनके सिस्टम में मूल्य निर्धारण की त्रुटि प्रतीत होती है, जानबूझकर की गई धोखाधड़ी नहीं। सर्वाधिक उपयुक्त कार्यवाही क्या है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Quietly switch to a different vendor without mentioning the overbilling, to avoid a difficult conversation.","hi":"कठिन बातचीत से बचने के लिए अधिक बिल का उल्लेख किए बिना चुपचाप दूसरे विक्रेता पर चले जाना।"},"2":{"en":"Contact the vendor to correct the discrepancy and request reimbursement.","hi":"विसंगति सुधारने के लिए विक्रेता से संपर्क करना और धनवापसी का अनुरोध करना।"},"3":{"en":"Absorb the cost as a loss since the hospital signed off on the invoices each time.","hi":"चूँकि अस्पताल ने हर बार बिल स्वीकृत किए थे, इसलिए राशि को हानि मानकर सहन कर लेना।"},"4":{"en":"Report the vendor to regulatory authorities immediately for fraudulent billing.","hi":"धोखाधड़ीपूर्ण बिलिंग के लिए विक्रेता की तुरंत नियामक प्राधिकरणों में शिकायत करना।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The overbilling is an error and not fraud, so the hospital is entitled to get the excess money back and the vendor needs to fix its system<br>Talking to the vendor about the discrepancy settles the money and prevents a repeat, which nobody else can do<br>Switching quietly loses the money, absorbing the loss rewards the error, and reporting fraud immediately is unfair when no fraud is suspected<br>So contacting the vendor and asking for reimbursement is the most appropriate action<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Contact the vendor to correct the discrepancy and request reimbursement..</b>","hi":"अधिक बिलिंग एक त्रुटि है, धोखाधड़ी नहीं, अतः अस्पताल को अतिरिक्त राशि वापस पाने का अधिकार है और विक्रेता को अपना सिस्टम सुधारना है<br>विक्रेता से विसंगति पर बात करने से राशि का समाधान होता है और पुनरावृत्ति रुकती है, जो कोई और नहीं कर सकता<br>चुपचाप विक्रेता बदलने से राशि चली जाती है, हानि सहन करने से त्रुटि को बढ़ावा मिलता है, तथा धोखाधड़ी की आशंका न होने पर तुरंत शिकायत करना अनुचित है<br>अतः विक्रेता से संपर्क करके धनवापसी का अनुरोध करना सर्वाधिक उपयुक्त कार्यवाही है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): विसंगति सुधारने के लिए विक्रेता से संपर्क करना और धनवापसी का अनुरोध करना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000073503","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the statement carefully and assume it to be true. Then examine the two conclusions given below it and decide which conclusion(s), if any, logically follow from the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>A multinational company has diversified its supply chain across multiple countries to reduce dependency on a single geographic production hub.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. The company has completely stopped production in its original country.<br>II. Diversification guarantees zero supply chain disruptions. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कथन को ध्यान से पढ़िए और उसे सत्य मानिए। फिर उसके नीचे दिए दो निष्कर्षों की जाँच कीजिए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सा/से निष्कर्ष कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलता/निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>एक बहुराष्ट्रीय कंपनी ने एक ही भौगोलिक उत्पादन केंद्र पर निर्भरता कम करने के लिए अपनी आपूर्ति शृंखला कई देशों में फैला दी है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. कंपनी ने अपने मूल देश में उत्पादन पूरी तरह बंद कर दिया है।<br>II. विविधीकरण आपूर्ति शृंखला में शून्य व्यवधान की गारंटी देता है। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor conclusion II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Diversifying the supply chain only means spreading production across more countries to reduce dependency; it does not say that production in the original country has stopped, so I does not follow<br>Spreading risk reduces the effect of a disruption but can never guarantee zero disruption, so II does not follow<br>Hence neither conclusion follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Neither conclusion I nor conclusion II follows.</b>","hi":"आपूर्ति शृंखला का विविधीकरण केवल यह बताता है कि निर्भरता कम करने के लिए उत्पादन अधिक देशों में फैलाया गया है; यह नहीं कहता कि मूल देश में उत्पादन बंद हो गया है, अतः I नहीं निकलता<br>जोखिम फैलाने से व्यवधान का प्रभाव घटता है, परंतु शून्य व्यवधान की गारंटी कभी नहीं दी जा सकती, अतः II भी नहीं निकलता<br>इसलिए कोई भी निष्कर्ष नहीं निकलता<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000073504","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"Read the given statement carefully and the following assumptions based on it. Decide which of the assumptions are implicit in the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>The victims of the imbalance in the industrial development are the large number of literate and illiterate people who are economically weak.<br><b>Assumptions:</b><br>I. Industrial development in India has taken place mainly on political considerations.<br>II. The tribals invariably get adversely affected by industrial development. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिया गया कथन तथा उस पर आधारित निम्नलिखित अवधारणाएँ ध्यान से पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सी अवधारणाएँ कथन में निहित हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>औद्योगिक विकास में असंतुलन के शिकार वे बड़ी संख्या में साक्षर तथा निरक्षर लोग हैं जो आर्थिक रूप से कमजोर हैं।<br><b>अवधारणाएँ:</b><br>I. भारत में औद्योगिक विकास मुख्यतः राजनीतिक विचारों पर हुआ है।<br>II. औद्योगिक विकास से आदिवासी अपरिवर्तनीय रूप से प्रतिकूल प्रभावित होते हैं। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Assumption I is implicit","hi":"केवल अवधारणा I निहित है"},"2":{"en":"Only Assumption II is implicit","hi":"केवल अवधारणा II निहित है"},"3":{"en":"Both Assumptions I and II are implicit","hi":"अवधारणा I और II दोनों निहित हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither Assumption I nor II is implicit","hi":"न तो अवधारणा I और न ही II निहित है"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The statement speaks only of the imbalance in industrial development and of the economically weak people who suffer from it; it says nothing about political considerations behind that development, so assumption I is not implicit<br>It also does not mention tribals at all, so assumption II is not implicit<br>Hence neither assumption is implicit<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Neither Assumption I nor II is implicit.</b>","hi":"कथन केवल औद्योगिक विकास में असंतुलन तथा उससे पीड़ित आर्थिक रूप से कमजोर लोगों की बात करता है; यह उस विकास के पीछे के राजनीतिक विचारों के बारे में कुछ नहीं कहता, अतः अवधारणा I निहित नहीं है<br>यह आदिवासियों का उल्लेख भी नहीं करता, अतः अवधारणा II भी निहित नहीं है<br>इसलिए कोई भी अवधारणा निहित नहीं है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): न तो अवधारणा I और न ही II निहित है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000073505","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Analogy","question":{"en":"Select the option that is related to the third word in the same way as the second word is related to the first word. (The words must be considered as meaningful English words and must not be related to each other based on the number of letters/number of consonants/vowels in the word.)<br>Joey : Kangaroo :: Cygnet : ? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"उस विकल्प का चयन कीजिए जो तीसरे शब्द से उसी प्रकार संबंधित है जिस प्रकार दूसरा शब्द पहले शब्द से संबंधित है। (शब्दों को अर्थपूर्ण अंग्रेज़ी शब्द मानना है और उनके अक्षरों की संख्या/व्यंजनों/स्वरों की संख्या के आधार पर परस्पर संबंध नहीं मानना है।)<br>Joey : Kangaroo :: Cygnet : ? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Duck"},"2":{"en":"Swan"},"3":{"en":"Goose"},"4":{"en":"Peacock"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"A joey is the young one of a kangaroo, so the pair shows the young one and its animal<br>A cygnet is the young one of a swan, so the third word is related to Swan in the same way<br>The young ones of a duck, a goose and a peacock are called duckling, gosling and peachick, so those words do not fit<br>Hence the answer is Swan<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Swan.</b>","hi":"जोई (Joey) कंगारू का शिशु है, अतः युग्म शिशु और उसके पशु का संबंध दर्शाता है<br>सिगनेट (Cygnet) राजहंस (Swan) का शिशु है, अतः तीसरा शब्द उसी प्रकार Swan से संबंधित है<br>बत्तख, हंस (Goose) तथा मोर के शिशुओं के नाम क्रमशः duckling, gosling तथा peachick हैं, अतः वे शब्द इस संबंध में नहीं बैठते<br>इसलिए उत्तर Swan है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): Swan है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000073506","section":"GK","topic":"Medieval History: The Mughal Empire","question":{"en":"Which among the following Mughal emperors did NOT pursue the policy of Sulh-i-Kul? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित मुगल सम्राटों में से किसने सुल्ह-ए-कुल की नीति का पालन नहीं किया? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Akbar","hi":"अकबर"},"2":{"en":"Jahangir","hi":"जहाँगीर"},"3":{"en":"Shah Jahan","hi":"शाहजहाँ"},"4":{"en":"Aurangzeb","hi":"औरंगज़ेब"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Aurangzeb</b><br><b>Aurangzeb</b> did not pursue the policy of <b>Sulh-i-Kul</b> (universal peace or tolerance) and instead reimposed the <b>jizya</b> on non-Muslims in 1679 and adopted a policy of religious orthodoxy.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Sulh-i-Kul</b> was propounded by <b>Akbar</b> and promoted by his ideal of religious tolerance through the Ibadat Khana and the Din-i-Ilahi.<br>• Akbar abolished the <b>jizya and pilgrimage tax</b>, married Rajput princesses and appointed Rajputs to high posts, following the policy of Sulh-i-Kul.<br>• <b>Jahangir</b> and <b>Shah Jahan</b> largely continued the liberal Mughal tradition, though Shah Jahan's reign was more orthodox in some respects.<br>• Aurangzeb's <b>Deccan campaigns, reimposition of jizya and temple destruction</b> marked a break from the policy of religious accommodation.<br><b>Correct option = (4)</b>, because Aurangzeb did not follow the policy of Sulh-i-Kul.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – औरंगज़ेब</b><br><b>औरंगज़ेब</b> ने <b>सुल्ह-ए-कुल</b> (सार्वभौम शांति या सहिष्णुता) की नीति का पालन नहीं किया और 1679 में गैर-मुस्लिमों पर <b>जजिया</b> पुनः लगाया तथा धार्मिक कट्टरता की नीति अपनाई।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>सुल्ह-ए-कुल</b> <b>अकबर</b> ने प्रतिपादित किया और इसे इबादत खाना तथा दीन-ए-इलाही के माध्यम से धार्मिक सहिष्णुता के आदर्श द्वारा बढ़ावा दिया।<br>• अकबर ने <b>जजिया तथा तीर्थयात्रा कर</b> समाप्त किए, राजपूत राजकुमारियों से विवाह किए तथा राजपूतों को उच्च पद दिए, जो सुल्ह-ए-कुल की नीति थी।<br>• <b>जहाँगीर</b> तथा <b>शाहजहाँ</b> ने मोटे तौर पर उदार मुगल परंपरा को जारी रखा, यद्यपि शाहजहाँ का शासन कुछ दृष्टियों से अधिक कट्टर था।<br>• औरंगज़ेब के <b>दक्कन अभियान, जजिया का पुनर्स्थापन तथा मंदिर विध्वंस</b> ने धार्मिक समन्वय की नीति से विचलन दर्शाया।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (4)</b>, क्योंकि औरंगज़ेब ने सुल्ह-ए-कुल की नीति का पालन नहीं किया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000073507","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: International News","question":{"en":"Chabahar Port lies on the coast. Which body of water does it lie on? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"चाबहार बंदरगाह तट पर स्थित है। यह किस जलनिकाय पर स्थित है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Red Sea","hi":"लाल सागर"},"2":{"en":"Arabian Sea","hi":"अरब सागर"},"3":{"en":"Persian Gulf","hi":"फारस की खाड़ी"},"4":{"en":"Gulf of Oman","hi":"ओमान की खाड़ी"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Gulf of Oman</b><br><b>Chabahar port</b> lies on the <b>Gulf of Oman</b>, on the Makran coast of Iran's Sistan-Baluchestan province, outside the Strait of Hormuz and on the Arabian Sea side.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Chabahar is Iran's only oceanic port, located about 170 km west of Pakistan's Gwadar port.<br>• It gives India access to Afghanistan and Central Asia through the <b>International North-South Transport Corridor</b>, bypassing Pakistan.<br>• India operates the <b>Shahid Beheshti terminal</b> at Chabahar and signed a ten-year agreement in 2024 through India Ports Global.<br>• The <b>Persian Gulf</b> lies to the west of Iran, and the Red Sea separates Africa from the Arabian Peninsula.<br><b>Correct option = (4)</b>, because Chabahar port lies on the Gulf of Oman.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – ओमान की खाड़ी</b><br><b>चाबहार बंदरगाह</b> ईरान के सिस्तान-बलूचिस्तान प्रांत के मकरान तट पर <b>ओमान की खाड़ी</b> पर स्थित है, जो होर्मुज जलडमरूमध्य के बाहर तथा अरब सागर की ओर है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• चाबहार ईरान का एकमात्र महासागरीय बंदरगाह है, जो पाकिस्तान के ग्वादर बंदरगाह से लगभग 170 किमी पश्चिम में है।<br>• यह भारत को <b>अंतरराष्ट्रीय उत्तर-दक्षिण परिवहन गलियारे</b> के माध्यम से पाकिस्तान से बचते हुए अफगानिस्तान तथा मध्य एशिया तक पहुँच देता है।<br>• भारत चाबहार के <b>शहीद बेहेश्ती टर्मिनल</b> का संचालन करता है और 2024 में इंडिया पोर्ट्स ग्लोबल के माध्यम से दस-वर्षीय समझौता किया।<br>• <b>फारस की खाड़ी</b> ईरान के पश्चिम में है, और लाल सागर अफ्रीका को अरब प्रायद्वीप से अलग करता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (4)</b>, क्योंकि चाबहार बंदरगाह ओमान की खाड़ी पर स्थित है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000073508","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Which Indian athlete is known as the \"Flying Sikh\"? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किस भारतीय खिलाड़ी को \"उड़न सिख\" (Flying Sikh) के नाम से जाना जाता है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"P.T. Usha","hi":"पी. टी. उषा"},"2":{"en":"Milkha Singh","hi":"मिल्खा सिंह"},"3":{"en":"Dhyan Chand","hi":"ध्यानचंद"},"4":{"en":"Sachin Tendulkar","hi":"सचिन तेंदुलकर"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Milkha Singh</b><br><b>Milkha Singh</b>, the legendary Indian sprinter, is known as the <b>'Flying Sikh'</b> for his speed on the track and his famous performances in the 200 m and 400 m events.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• He finished <b>fourth in the 400 m final</b> at the Rome Olympics 1960, missing a medal narrowly, and won gold in the 400 m at the <b>1958 Asian Games and Commonwealth Games</b>.<br>• He set a national record in the 400 m that stood for decades and was awarded the <b>Padma Shri</b>.<br>• His life is the subject of the film 'Bhaag Milkha Bhaag'.<br>• <b>P.T. Usha</b> is called the 'Payyoli Express', <b>Dhyan Chand</b> the 'Wizard of Hockey' and <b>Sachin Tendulkar</b> the 'Little Master'.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because Milkha Singh is known as the Flying Sikh.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – मिल्खा सिंह</b><br>महान भारतीय धावक <b>मिल्खा सिंह (Milkha Singh)</b> को ट्रैक पर उनकी गति तथा 200 मीटर एवं 400 मीटर स्पर्धाओं में प्रसिद्ध प्रदर्शन के कारण <b>'उड़न सिख'</b> कहा जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• वे <b>रोम ओलंपिक 1960</b> की 400 मीटर स्पर्धा के फाइनल में <b>चौथे स्थान</b> पर रहे और पदक से थोड़ा चूक गए, तथा <b>1958 के एशियाई खेलों और राष्ट्रमंडल खेलों</b> में 400 मीटर में स्वर्ण जीता।<br>• उन्होंने 400 मीटर में राष्ट्रीय कीर्तिमान बनाया जो दशकों तक कायम रहा, और उन्हें <b>पद्म श्री</b> प्रदान किया गया।<br>• उनके जीवन पर फिल्म 'भाग मिल्खा भाग' बनी।<br>• <b>पी. टी. उषा</b> को 'पय्योली एक्सप्रेस', <b>ध्यानचंद</b> को 'हॉकी का जादूगर' तथा <b>सचिन तेंदुलकर</b> को 'लिटिल मास्टर' कहा जाता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि मिल्खा सिंह को उड़न सिख कहा जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000073509","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Awards and Honours","question":{"en":"Which of the following Indian authors has never won the Sahitya Akademi Award or the Padma Awards as of 2023? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित भारतीय लेखकों में से किसने 2023 तक साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार या पद्म पुरस्कार कभी नहीं जीता? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"R.K. Narayan","hi":"आर. के. नारायण"},"2":{"en":"Salman Rushdie","hi":"सलमान रुश्दी"},"3":{"en":"Amitav Ghosh","hi":"अमिताव घोष"},"4":{"en":"Mahasweta Devi","hi":"महाश्वेता देवी"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Salman Rushdie</b><br><b>Salman Rushdie</b> has not received the <b>Sahitya Akademi Award</b> or any <b>Padma award</b> as of 2023, although he has won the Booker Prize, the Booker of Bookers and many international honours.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>R.K. Narayan</b> received the Sahitya Akademi Award (1958) and the Padma Vibhushan (2001).<br>• <b>Amitav Ghosh</b> won the Sahitya Akademi Award (1989) and the Jnanpith Award (2024), and <b>Mahasweta Devi</b> received both the Sahitya Akademi Award (1979) and the Jnanpith (1996) along with the Padma Vibhushan.<br>• The <b>Sahitya Akademi Award</b> is given for outstanding literary work in any of the 24 recognised Indian languages.<br>• Rushdie's work is written in English and he has lived mostly abroad since 1989, which is part of the reason he has not received these Indian awards.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because Salman Rushdie has won neither a Sahitya Akademi Award nor a Padma award.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – सलमान रुश्दी</b><br><b>सलमान रुश्दी</b> को 2023 तक <b>साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार</b> अथवा कोई <b>पद्म पुरस्कार</b> नहीं मिला, यद्यपि उन्हें बुकर पुरस्कार, बुकर ऑफ बुकर्स तथा अनेक अंतरराष्ट्रीय सम्मान प्राप्त हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>आर. के. नारायण</b> को साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार (1958) तथा पद्म विभूषण (2001) मिला।<br>• <b>अमिताव घोष</b> ने साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार (1989) तथा ज्ञानपीठ पुरस्कार (2024) जीता, और <b>महाश्वेता देवी</b> को साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार (1979), ज्ञानपीठ (1996) तथा पद्म विभूषण मिला।<br>• <b>साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार</b> 24 मान्यता प्राप्त भारतीय भाषाओं में से किसी में उत्कृष्ट साहित्यिक कृति के लिए दिया जाता है।<br>• रुश्दी की रचनाएँ अंग्रेज़ी में हैं और 1989 के बाद वे अधिकांशतः विदेश में रहे, जो इन भारतीय पुरस्कारों से वंचित रहने का एक कारण है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि सलमान रुश्दी को न साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार मिला न पद्म पुरस्कार।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000073510","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Five Year Plan and Industrial Policy Resolution","question":{"en":"During which of the following was the enactment of the Industrial Development and Regulation Act (IDRA) of 1951, aimed at regulating India’s industrial sector? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत के औद्योगिक क्षेत्र के नियमन हेतु औद्योगिक विकास एवं नियमन अधिनियम (IDRA), 1951 का अधिनियमन निम्नलिखित में से किसके काल में हुआ? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"First Five-Year Plan","hi":"प्रथम पंचवर्षीय योजना"},"2":{"en":"Second Five-Year Plan","hi":"द्वितीय पंचवर्षीय योजना"},"3":{"en":"Third Five-Year Plan","hi":"तृतीय पंचवर्षीय योजना"},"4":{"en":"Fourth Five-Year Plan","hi":"चतुर्थ पंचवर्षीय योजना"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – First Five-Year Plan</b><br>The <b>Industrial (Development and Regulation) Act, 1951</b> was enacted during the period of the <b>First Five-Year Plan (1951-56)</b>, providing the legal framework for licensing and regulation of industries in India.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The IDRA required industrial undertakings to obtain a <b>licence</b> for manufacturing, and gave the government powers over location, capacity and expansion.<br>• It was accompanied by the <b>Industries (Development and Regulation) Act schedule</b> listing scheduled industries and by the <b>Industrial Policy Resolution of 1956</b>, which divided industries into three schedules.<br>• The First Plan itself focused on <b>agriculture and irrigation</b>, while the Second Plan (1956-61) emphasised heavy industry.<br>• The IDRA was substantially liberalised after <b>1991</b>, when industrial licensing was abolished for most industries.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because IDRA 1951 was enacted during the First Five-Year Plan.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – प्रथम पंचवर्षीय योजना</b><br><b>औद्योगिक (विकास एवं नियमन) अधिनियम, 1951</b> <b>प्रथम पंचवर्षीय योजना (1951-56)</b> के काल में अधिनियमित हुआ, जिसने भारत में उद्योगों के लाइसेंसन तथा नियमन का विधिक ढाँचा दिया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• IDRA के अंतर्गत औद्योगिक उपक्रमों को निर्माण हेतु <b>लाइसेंस</b> लेना आवश्यक था, और सरकार को स्थान, क्षमता तथा विस्तार पर शक्तियाँ प्राप्त थीं।<br>• इसके साथ अनुसूचित उद्योगों की सूची तथा <b>औद्योगिक नीति संकल्प, 1956</b> आया, जिसने उद्योगों को तीन अनुसूचियों में विभाजित किया।<br>• प्रथम योजना स्वयं <b>कृषि तथा सिंचाई</b> पर केंद्रित थी, जबकि द्वितीय योजना (1956-61) ने भारी उद्योग पर बल दिया।<br>• <b>1991</b> के बाद IDRA में व्यापक उदारीकरण हुआ, जब अधिकांश उद्योगों के लिए औद्योगिक लाइसेंसिंग समाप्त कर दी गई।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि IDRA 1951 प्रथम पंचवर्षीय योजना के काल में अधिनियमित हुआ।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000073511","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"What is the line that a Kabaddi raider must cross to be considered safe in the opponent’s territory called? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कबड्डी में प्रतिद्वंद्वी के क्षेत्र में सुरक्षित माने जाने हेतु रेडर को जिस रेखा को पार करना होता है, उसे क्या कहा जाता है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Lobby line","hi":"लॉबी रेखा"},"2":{"en":"Baulk line","hi":"बॉक रेखा (Baulk line)"},"3":{"en":"Bonus line","hi":"बोनस रेखा"},"4":{"en":"Mid-line","hi":"मध्य रेखा"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Baulk line</b><br>In kabaddi the raider must <b>cross the baulk line</b> in the opponent's court and return to his own half without losing breath to complete a successful raid and earn a point.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Kabaddi's court is divided by a <b>mid-line</b>, and each half has a <b>baulk line</b> and a <b>bonus line</b>.<br>• Touching the <b>bonus line</b> while crossing the baulk line earns an extra point for the raider.<br>• The <b>lobby</b> is the strip outside the playing area, and the raider must keep chanting 'kabaddi' continuously.<br>• A raid lasts a maximum of <b>30 seconds</b>, and the team with more points at the end wins the match.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because the raider must cross the baulk line in the opponent's territory.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – बॉक रेखा (Baulk line)</b><br>कबड्डी में रेडर को सफल रेड करके अंक पाने के लिए प्रतिद्वंद्वी के कोर्ट में <b>बॉक रेखा पार करनी</b> होती है और बिना साँस टूटे अपने आधे भाग में लौटना होता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• कबड्डी का कोर्ट <b>मध्य रेखा</b> से विभाजित होता है और प्रत्येक आधे भाग में <b>बॉक रेखा</b> तथा <b>बोनस रेखा</b> होती है।<br>• बॉक रेखा पार करते समय <b>बोनस रेखा</b> छूने पर रेडर को अतिरिक्त अंक मिलता है।<br>• <b>लॉबी</b> खेल क्षेत्र के बाहर की पट्टी है, और रेडर को लगातार 'कबड्डी' का उच्चारण करना होता है।<br>• एक रेड अधिकतम <b>30 सेकंड</b> की होती है, और अंत में अधिक अंक वाली टीम जीतती है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि रेडर को प्रतिद्वंद्वी के क्षेत्र में बॉक रेखा पार करनी होती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000073512","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Which Indian sportsperson is nicknamed “Golden Girl”? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किस भारतीय खिलाड़ी को \"गोल्डन गर्ल\" के उपनाम से जाना जाता है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"PT Usha","hi":"पी. टी. उषा"},"2":{"en":"Mary Kom","hi":"मैरी कॉम"},"3":{"en":"Sania Mirza","hi":"सानिया मिर्ज़ा"},"4":{"en":"Saina Nehwal","hi":"साइना नेहवाल"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – PT Usha</b><br><b>P.T. Usha</b>, the legendary Indian sprinter and hurdler, is popularly called the <b>'Golden Girl'</b> of Indian athletics for her record-breaking performances in the 1980s.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• She won <b>four gold medals and one silver</b> at the 1985 Asian Athletics Championships and dominated the 1982 and 1986 Asian Games.<br>• At the <b>1984 Los Angeles Olympics</b> she missed the 400 m hurdles bronze by one-hundredth of a second.<br>• She was the first Indian woman to reach an Olympic final and was awarded the <b>Padma Shri and Arjuna Award</b>.<br>• She later became a coach and was nominated to the Rajya Sabha, and was awarded the Padma Bhushan.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because P.T. Usha is known as the Golden Girl of Indian athletics.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – पी. टी. उषा</b><br>महान भारतीय धाविका तथा बाधा-दौड़ खिलाड़ी <b>पी. टी. उषा (P.T. Usha)</b> को 1980 के दशक के कीर्तिमानी प्रदर्शनों के कारण भारतीय एथलेटिक्स की <b>'गोल्डन गर्ल'</b> कहा जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• उन्होंने 1985 की एशियाई एथलेटिक्स चैंपियनशिप में <b>चार स्वर्ण तथा एक रजत</b> जीता और 1982 एवं 1986 के एशियाई खेलों में दबदबा रखा।<br>• <b>1984 के लॉस एंजिल्स ओलंपिक</b> में वे 400 मीटर बाधा दौड़ में एक सेकंड के सौवें भाग से कांस्य से चूकीं।<br>• वे ओलंपिक फाइनल में पहुँचने वाली प्रथम भारतीय महिला थीं और उन्हें <b>पद्म श्री तथा अर्जुन पुरस्कार</b> मिला।<br>• बाद में वे प्रशिक्षक बनीं, राज्यसभा के लिए मनोनीत हुईं और उन्हें पद्म भूषण प्रदान किया गया।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि पी. टी. उषा को भारतीय एथलेटिक्स की गोल्डन गर्ल कहा जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000073513","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Folk Dances and Festivals","question":{"en":"The Baisakhi Mela in Haryana marks the start of which harvest season? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"हरियाणा का बैसाखी मेला किस फसल मौसम के आरंभ का प्रतीक है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Kharif","hi":"खरीफ"},"2":{"en":"Rabi","hi":"रबी"},"3":{"en":"Summer","hi":"ग्रीष्मकाल"},"4":{"en":"Winter","hi":"शीतकाल"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Rabi</b><br>The <b>Baisakhi Mela</b> in Haryana, celebrated in April, marks the <b>harvest of the rabi crop</b> and the beginning of the new agricultural year, along with the solar new year of the Bikrami calendar.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Baisakhi is celebrated on <b>13 or 14 April</b> with fairs at places such as <b>Baisakhia village near Yamunanagar</b> and Kurukshetra.<br>• <b>Rabi crops</b> such as wheat, barley, gram and mustard are sown in October-December and harvested in April, giving the festival its significance.<br>• Baisakhi also commemorates the <b>founding of the Khalsa by Guru Gobind Singh in 1699</b>.<br>• Kharif crops are harvested around October with festivals such as Diwali and Navaratri, not Baisakhi.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because the Baisakhi Mela marks the rabi harvest season.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – रबी</b><br>हरियाणा में अप्रैल में मनाया जाने वाला <b>बैसाखी मेला</b> <b>रबी फसल की कटाई</b> तथा नए कृषि वर्ष के आरंभ का प्रतीक है, साथ ही विक्रमी पंचांग के सौर नववर्ष का भी।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• बैसाखी <b>13 या 14 अप्रैल</b> को मनाई जाती है, और <b>यमुनानगर के निकट बैसाखिया गाँव</b> तथा कुरुक्षेत्र जैसे स्थानों पर मेले लगते हैं।<br>• <b>रबी फसलें</b> जैसे गेहूँ, जौ, चना तथा सरसों अक्टूबर-दिसंबर में बोई और अप्रैल में काटी जाती हैं, जिससे इस उत्सव का महत्व बनता है।<br>• बैसाखी <b>1699 में गुरु गोबिंद सिंह द्वारा खालसा की स्थापना</b> की भी स्मृति है।<br>• खरीफ फसल की कटाई अक्टूबर के आसपास दिवाली तथा नवरात्रि जैसे उत्सवों के साथ होती है, बैसाखी के साथ नहीं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि बैसाखी मेला रबी कटाई मौसम का प्रतीक है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000073514","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"Under the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, what is the punishment for cyber stalking? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारतीय न्याय संहिता, 2023 के अंतर्गत साइबर स्टॉकिंग के लिए दंड क्या है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Imprisonment for life","hi":"आजीवन कारावास"},"2":{"en":"Imprisonment up to 1 year","hi":"एक वर्ष तक का कारावास"},"3":{"en":"Imprisonment up to 3 years and a fine","hi":"तीन वर्ष तक का कारावास तथा जुर्माना"},"4":{"en":"A fine of ₹1 lakh","hi":"₹1 लाख का जुर्माना"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Imprisonment up to 3 years and a fine</b><br>Under the <b>Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023</b>, <b>stalking including cyber stalking</b> is punishable with <b>imprisonment up to three years and a fine</b> for the first conviction, and up to five years for a second conviction.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Section 78</b> of the BNS deals with stalking, including following a woman, contacting her against her wishes through any electronic means and monitoring her internet or email use.<br>• The offence is <b>cognizable, non-bailable and non-compoundable</b>, and exceptions apply where the conduct was pursued to prevent serious harm.<br>• Related offences include <b>voyeurism (Section 77) and sexual harassment (Section 75)</b>, which also cover digital conduct.<br>• The BNS replaced Section 354D of the IPC and reflects the growing recognition of online harassment of women.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because cyber stalking is punishable with up to three years' imprisonment and a fine.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – तीन वर्ष तक का कारावास तथा जुर्माना</b><br><b>भारतीय न्याय संहिता, 2023</b> के अंतर्गत <b>पीछा करना, जिसमें साइबर स्टॉकिंग भी सम्मिलित है</b>, प्रथम दोषसिद्धि पर <b>तीन वर्ष तक कारावास तथा जुर्माने</b> से दंडनीय है, और द्वितीय दोषसिद्धि पर पाँच वर्ष तक।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• BNS की <b>धारा 78</b> पीछा करने से संबंधित है, जिसमें महिला के पीछे चलना, किसी भी इलेक्ट्रॉनिक माध्यम से उसकी इच्छा के विरुद्ध संपर्क करना तथा उसके इंटरनेट या ईमेल उपयोग पर निगरानी रखना सम्मिलित है।<br>• यह अपराध <b>संज्ञेय, गैर-जमानती तथा गैर-समझौतायोग्य</b> है, और गंभीर हानि रोकने के उद्देश्य से किए गए कृत्य पर अपवाद लागू होते हैं।<br>• संबंधित अपराधों में <b>निरीक्षण-दोष (धारा 77) तथा यौन उत्पीड़न (धारा 75)</b> सम्मिलित हैं, जो डिजिटल आचरण को भी समेटते हैं।<br>• BNS ने IPC की धारा 354D का स्थान लिया और महिलाओं के ऑनलाइन उत्पीड़न की बढ़ती मान्यता को दर्शाती है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि साइबर स्टॉकिंग पर तीन वर्ष तक कारावास तथा जुर्माना है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000073515","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Socio Religious Reforms","question":{"en":"Andhra Mahila Sabha was founded by which of the following Indian freedom fighters to provide education to women? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"आंध्र महिला सभा की स्थापना किस भारतीय स्वतंत्रता सेनानी ने महिलाओं को शिक्षा देने के लिए की? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rukmini Lakshmipathi","hi":"रुक्मिणी लक्ष्मीपति"},"2":{"en":"Chityala Ilamma","hi":"चित्याला इलम्मा"},"3":{"en":"Baru Alivelamma","hi":"बारू अलिवेलम्मा"},"4":{"en":"Durgabai Deshmukh","hi":"दुर्गाबाई देशमुख"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Durgabai Deshmukh</b><br>The <b>Andhra Mahila Sabha</b> was founded by <b>Durgabai Deshmukh</b> in 1938 at Madras to promote <b>education and welfare of women</b>, and it grew into a large network of schools, colleges and hospitals.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Durgabai Deshmukh was a freedom fighter, lawyer and member of the Constituent Assembly, and she chaired the <b>Central Social Welfare Board</b>.<br>• She is known as the <b>'builder of institutions'</b> and was awarded the <b>Padma Vibhushan</b>; she founded the Andhra Mahila Sabha and the Council for Social Development.<br>• She participated in the <b>Salt Satyagraha</b> and was imprisoned, and later served as a member of the Planning Commission.<br>• <b>Rukmini Lakshmipathi</b> was a Congress leader and the first woman minister in Madras Province, and <b>Chityala Ilamma</b> was a peasant leader of Telangana.<br><b>Correct option = (4)</b>, because Durgabai Deshmukh founded the Andhra Mahila Sabha.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – दुर्गाबाई देशमुख</b><br><b>आंध्र महिला सभा</b> की स्थापना <b>दुर्गाबाई देशमुख</b> ने 1938 में मद्रास में <b>महिलाओं की शिक्षा तथा कल्याण</b> को बढ़ावा देने के लिए की, और यह विद्यालयों, महाविद्यालयों एवं अस्पतालों का बड़ा नेटवर्क बन गई।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• दुर्गाबाई देशमुख स्वतंत्रता सेनानी, विधिवेत्ता तथा संविधान सभा की सदस्य थीं, और उन्होंने <b>केंद्रीय समाज कल्याण बोर्ड</b> की अध्यक्षता की।<br>• उन्हें <b>'संस्थाओं की निर्माता'</b> कहा जाता है और उन्हें <b>पद्म विभूषण</b> मिला; उन्होंने आंध्र महिला सभा तथा काउंसिल फॉर सोशल डेवलपमेंट की स्थापना की।<br>• उन्होंने <b>नमक सत्याग्रह</b> में भाग लिया और कारावास भोगा, तथा बाद में योजना आयोग की सदस्य रहीं।<br>• <b>रुक्मिणी लक्ष्मीपति</b> कांग्रेस नेता तथा मद्रास प्रांत की प्रथम महिला मंत्री थीं, और <b>चित्याला इलम्मा</b> तेलंगाना की किसान नेता थीं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (4)</b>, क्योंकि आंध्र महिला सभा की संस्थापक दुर्गाबाई देशमुख थीं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000073516","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Music and Musical Instruments","question":{"en":"Who among the following artists, known for his mastery of the percussion instrument Chenda, was a recipient of the Sangeet Natak Akademi Award for the year 2023? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित कलाकारों में से कौन ताल वाद्य चेंडा में महारत के लिए जाने जाते हैं तथा वर्ष 2023 के संगीत नाटक अकादमी पुरस्कार के प्राप्तकर्ता रहे? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Gopalan Nair Venu","hi":"गोपालन नायर वेणु"},"2":{"en":"C. Kunhirama Marar","hi":"सी. कुंहिरामा मारार"},"3":{"en":"Niladri Kumar","hi":"निलाद्रि कुमार"},"4":{"en":"Perini Prakash","hi":"पेरिनी प्रकाश"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – C. Kunhirama Marar</b><br><b>C. (Cheruthazham) Kunhirama Marar</b> received the <b>Sangeet Natak Akademi Award for 2023</b> for his mastery of the <b>chenda</b>, the cylindrical percussion instrument central to Kerala's temple rituals and performances.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>chenda</b> is a cylindrical drum played with sticks and is essential to <b>Kathakali, Theyyam, Koodiyattam and temple festivals</b>; its playing style is called 'chenda melam'.<br>• The Akademi Awards for 2022 and 2023 were conferred by President Droupadi Murmu in March 2024.<br>• <b>Gopalan Nair Venu</b> received the 2023 award for overall contribution and scholarship in performing arts, particularly Koodiyattam.<br>• <b>Niladri Kumar</b> is a sitar player who received the 2023 award for creative and experimental music, and <b>Perini Prakash</b> received it for scholarship in performing arts.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because C. Kunhirama Marar was honoured for Chenda in 2023.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – सी. कुंहिरामा मारार</b><br><b>सी. (चेरुथाझम) कुंहिरामा मारार</b> को <b>चेंडा</b> में महारत के लिए <b>वर्ष 2023 का संगीत नाटक अकादमी पुरस्कार</b> मिला, जो केरल के मंदिर अनुष्ठानों तथा प्रस्तुतियों का केंद्रीय ताल वाद्य है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>चेंडा</b> डंडियों से बजाया जाने वाला बेलनाकार ढोल है और यह <b>कथकली, थेय्यम, कूडियाट्टम तथा मंदिर उत्सवों</b> का अनिवार्य अंग है; इसकी वादन शैली 'चेंडा मेलम' कहलाती है।<br>• 2022 तथा 2023 के अकादमी पुरस्कार राष्ट्रपति द्रौपदी मुर्मू ने मार्च 2024 में प्रदान किए।<br>• <b>गोपालन नायर वेणु</b> को प्रदर्शन कलाओं में समग्र योगदान तथा विद्वत्ता, विशेषतः कूडियाट्टम के लिए 2023 का पुरस्कार मिला।<br>• <b>निलाद्रि कुमार</b> सितार वादक हैं जिन्हें सृजनात्मक एवं प्रयोगात्मक संगीत के लिए तथा <b>पेरिनी प्रकाश</b> को प्रदर्शन कलाओं की विद्वत्ता के लिए 2023 का पुरस्कार मिला।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि सी. कुंहिरामा मारार को 2023 में चेंडा के लिए सम्मानित किया गया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000073517","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Forest and Grassland","question":{"en":"Which of the following is/are regions of tropical forest and mangroves?<br><br>Select the CORRECT answer using codes given below.<br>1. Western Ghats<br>2. Andaman Nicobar Islands<br>3. West Bengal [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन उष्णकटिबंधीय वन तथा मैंग्रोव के क्षेत्र है/हैं?<br><br>नीचे दिए गए कूटों का उपयोग करके सही उत्तर चुनें।<br>1. पश्चिमी घाट<br>2. अंडमान निकोबार द्वीपसमूह<br>3. पश्चिम बंगाल [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3 only","hi":"केवल 3"},"2":{"en":"1 and 2 only","hi":"केवल 1 तथा 2"},"3":{"en":"2 and 3 only","hi":"केवल 2 तथा 3"},"4":{"en":"All of these","hi":"ये सभी"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – All of these</b><br>All three regions have tropical forests and mangroves – the <b>Western Ghats</b> have tropical evergreen and semi-evergreen forests, the <b>Andaman and Nicobar Islands</b> have tropical rainforests and mangroves, and <b>West Bengal</b> has the Sundarbans, the world's largest mangrove forest.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Mangroves</b> are salt-tolerant forests of the intertidal zone with stilt roots and viviparous seeds, found along sheltered tropical coasts.<br>• The <b>Sundarbans</b> in the Ganga-Brahmaputra delta is a UNESCO World Heritage site and the habitat of the Royal Bengal tiger.<br>• India's mangrove cover is largest in <b>West Bengal, Gujarat, Andaman and Nicobar Islands and Andhra Pradesh</b>.<br>• Tropical evergreen forests occur where rainfall exceeds 200 cm, as in the Western Ghats, the north-east and the Andaman and Nicobar Islands.<br><b>Correct option = (4)</b>, because all the listed regions have tropical forests and mangroves.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – ये सभी</b><br>तीनों क्षेत्रों में उष्णकटिबंधीय वन तथा मैंग्रोव हैं – <b>पश्चिमी घाट</b> में उष्णकटिबंधीय सदाबहार एवं अर्ध-सदाबहार वन, <b>अंडमान एवं निकोबार द्वीपसमूह</b> में उष्णकटिबंधीय वर्षावन तथा मैंग्रोव, और <b>पश्चिम बंगाल</b> में विश्व का सबसे बड़ा मैंग्रोव वन <b>सुंदरबन</b> है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>मैंग्रोव</b> ज्वारीय क्षेत्र के लवण-सहिष्णु वन हैं, जिनमें स्टिल्ट जड़ें तथा जरायुज बीज होते हैं और जो संरक्षित उष्णकटिबंधीय तटों पर मिलते हैं।<br>• गंगा-ब्रह्मपुत्र डेल्टा का <b>सुंदरबन</b> यूनेस्को विश्व धरोहर स्थल तथा रॉयल बंगाल टाइगर का आवास है।<br>• भारत में मैंग्रोव आवरण <b>पश्चिम बंगाल, गुजरात, अंडमान एवं निकोबार द्वीपसमूह तथा आंध्र प्रदेश</b> में सर्वाधिक है।<br>• उष्णकटिबंधीय सदाबहार वन वहाँ होते हैं जहाँ वर्षा 200 सेमी से अधिक हो, जैसे पश्चिमी घाट, पूर्वोत्तर तथा अंडमान एवं निकोबार द्वीपसमूह।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (4)</b>, क्योंकि सभी उल्लिखित क्षेत्रों में उष्णकटिबंधीय वन तथा मैंग्रोव हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000073518","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Gupta Dynasty","question":{"en":"Which Gupta dynasty's fiscal term is correctly matched with its meaning? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"गुप्त राजवंश के किस राजकोषीय शब्द का उसके अर्थ से सही मेल है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Dhanya – levy on precious metals","hi":"धान्य – बहुमूल्य धातुओं पर उपकर"},"2":{"en":"Hiranya – gold/cash tax","hi":"हिरण्य – स्वर्ण/नकद कर"},"3":{"en":"Vaishthika – share of produce","hi":"वैष्ठिक – उपज का भाग"},"4":{"en":"Bhaga – penalty for offences","hi":"भाग – अपराधों पर दंड"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Hiranya – gold/cash tax</b><br>In Gupta inscriptions, <b>hiranya</b> denotes a tax payable in <b>gold or cash</b>, while <b>dhanya</b> is a tax paid in <b>kind, usually a share of grain</b>, and <b>bhaga</b> is the king's share of produce.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Bhaga</b> was normally <b>one-sixth of the produce</b>, and <b>bhoga</b> was a periodical supply of fruits, flowers and other articles to the king.<br>• <b>Hiranya</b> was levied in cash and is mentioned in the Poona and Kathiawar plates, showing the monetisation of the Gupta economy.<br>• <b>Udranga</b> and <b>uparikara</b> were land taxes, and <b>halivakara</b> was probably a plough tax.<br>• The term 'vaishthika' relates to artisans or guilds, not to a share of produce.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because hiranya means a tax paid in gold or cash.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – हिरण्य – स्वर्ण/नकद कर</b><br>गुप्त अभिलेखों में <b>हिरण्य</b> से तात्पर्य <b>स्वर्ण या नकद</b> में देय कर से है, जबकि <b>धान्य</b> वस्तु रूप में, सामान्यतः अनाज के भाग के रूप में दिया जाने वाला कर है, और <b>भाग</b> राजा का उपज में हिस्सा है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>भाग</b> सामान्यतः <b>उपज का छठा भाग</b> होता था, तथा <b>भोग</b> राजा को फल, फूल तथा अन्य वस्तुओं की आवधिक आपूर्ति थी।<br>• <b>हिरण्य</b> नकद में लिया जाता था और इसका उल्लेख पूना तथा काठियावाड़ ताम्रपत्रों में मिलता है, जो गुप्त अर्थव्यवस्था के मुद्रीकरण को दर्शाता है।<br>• <b>उद्रंग</b> तथा <b>उपरिकर</b> भूमि कर थे, और <b>हलिवाकर</b> संभवतः हल कर था।<br>• 'वैष्ठिक' शब्द शिल्पियों या श्रेणियों से संबंधित है, उपज के भाग से नहीं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि हिरण्य स्वर्ण या नकद में दिया जाने वाला कर है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000073519","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: International News","question":{"en":"What is the proposed technology for the UAE–India power link under IMEC (India–Middle East–Europe Economic Corridor)? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"IMEC (भारत–मध्य पूर्व–यूरोप आर्थिक गलियारा) के अंतर्गत UAE–भारत विद्युत संपर्क हेतु प्रस्तावित प्रौद्योगिकी क्या है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Medium-voltage AC","hi":"मध्यम वोल्टेज AC"},"2":{"en":"High-voltage bipolar DC","hi":"उच्च वोल्टेज द्विध्रुवी DC"},"3":{"en":"Subsea superconducting line","hi":"समुद्रगामी अतिचालक लाइन"},"4":{"en":"Standard DC overhead line","hi":"मानक DC ओवरहेड लाइन"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – High-voltage bipolar DC</b><br>The proposed <b>UAE-India power link</b> under <b>IMEC (India-Middle East-Europe Economic Corridor)</b> envisages a subsea <b>high-voltage direct current (HVDC) bipolar</b> transmission line to carry electricity over long distances with lower losses.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>HVDC</b> is preferred over AC for long subsea cables because of lower transmission losses and no reactive power problems.<br>• IMEC was announced at the <b>G20 Summit in New Delhi in September 2023</b>, with India, the UAE, Saudi Arabia, the EU, France, Germany, Italy and the USA as partners.<br>• The corridor combines a <b>rail and shipping route, an electricity cable, a hydrogen pipeline and a data cable</b> between India, the Gulf and Europe.<br>• The link would connect India's west coast to the UAE across the Arabian Sea, complementing projects like One Sun One World One Grid.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because the proposed technology is high-voltage bipolar DC.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – उच्च वोल्टेज द्विध्रुवी DC</b><br><b>IMEC (भारत-मध्य पूर्व-यूरोप आर्थिक गलियारा)</b> के अंतर्गत प्रस्तावित <b>UAE-भारत विद्युत संपर्क</b> में लंबी दूरी तक कम हानि के साथ बिजली पहुँचाने हेतु समुद्रगामी <b>उच्च वोल्टेज प्रत्यक्ष धारा (HVDC) द्विध्रुवी</b> संचरण लाइन की परिकल्पना है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• लंबी समुद्री केबलों के लिए <b>HVDC</b> को AC की तुलना में वरीयता दी जाती है, क्योंकि संचरण हानि कम होती है और प्रतिघाती शक्ति की समस्या नहीं होती।<br>• IMEC की घोषणा <b>सितंबर 2023 में नई दिल्ली के G20 शिखर सम्मेलन</b> में हुई, जिसमें भारत, UAE, सऊदी अरब, यूरोपीय संघ, फ्रांस, जर्मनी, इटली तथा अमेरिका साझेदार हैं।<br>• यह गलियारा भारत, खाड़ी तथा यूरोप के बीच <b>रेल एवं शिपिंग मार्ग, विद्युत केबल, हाइड्रोजन पाइपलाइन तथा डेटा केबल</b> को जोड़ता है।<br>• यह लिंक अरब सागर के रास्ते भारत के पश्चिमी तट को UAE से जोड़ेगा और वन सन वन वर्ल्ड वन ग्रिड जैसी परियोजनाओं का पूरक होगा।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि प्रस्तावित प्रौद्योगिकी उच्च वोल्टेज द्विध्रुवी DC है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000073520","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Books and Authors","question":{"en":"Which of the following best describes the literary significance of 'Diary of a Malayali Madman' by N. Prabhakaran and Jayasree Kalathil? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एन. प्रभाकरन तथा जयश्री कलाथिल द्वारा 'डायरी ऑफ ए मलयाली मैडमैन' के साहित्यिक महत्व का सर्वोत्तम वर्णन कौन-सा है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Acclaimed Malayalam work with cultural insights","hi":"सांस्कृतिक अंतर्दृष्टि युक्त प्रशंसित मलयालम कृति"},"2":{"en":"Historical novel about Kerala’s ancient kingdoms","hi":"केरल के प्राचीन राज्यों पर ऐतिहासिक उपन्यास"},"3":{"en":"Collection of political essays on Kerala governance","hi":"केरल के शासन पर राजनीतिक निबंधों का संग्रह"},"4":{"en":"Translation of Sanskrit poetry into Malayalam","hi":"संस्कृत कविता का मलयालम अनुवाद"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Acclaimed Malayalam work with cultural insights</b><br><b>'Diary of a Malayali Madman'</b> is a collection of stories by the acclaimed Malayalam writer <b>N. Prabhakaran</b>, translated into English by <b>Jayasree Kalathil</b>, and is valued for its <b>experimental style and sharp cultural insights</b> into Kerala society.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• N. Prabhakaran is a major contemporary Malayalam writer known for novels such as <b>'Daivathinte Pusthakam'</b> and short-story collections.<br>• <b>Jayasree Kalathil</b> is a translator and mental health researcher whose translations of Malayalam and Kashmiri literature have won international recognition.<br>• The stories in the book deal with <b>madness, desire, caste and everyday life in Kerala</b>, presented through unconventional narration.<br>• The book is a work of translation from Malayalam, not of Sanskrit poetry, and it is fiction, not a history or a collection of political essays.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because the book is an acclaimed Malayalam work with cultural insights.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – सांस्कृतिक अंतर्दृष्टि युक्त प्रशंसित मलयालम कृति</b><br><b>'डायरी ऑफ ए मलयाली मैडमैन'</b> प्रतिष्ठित मलयालम लेखक <b>एन. प्रभाकरन</b> की कहानियों का संग्रह है, जिसका अंग्रेज़ी अनुवाद <b>जयश्री कलाथिल</b> ने किया, और इसे केरल समाज पर <b>प्रयोगात्मक शैली तथा तीक्ष्ण सांस्कृतिक अंतर्दृष्टि</b> के लिए सराहा जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• एन. प्रभाकरन समकालीन मलयालम के प्रमुख लेखक हैं, जो <b>'दैवथिंते पुस्तकम्'</b> जैसे उपन्यासों तथा कहानी संग्रहों के लिए जाने जाते हैं।<br>• <b>जयश्री कलाथिल</b> अनुवादक तथा मानसिक स्वास्थ्य शोधकर्ता हैं, जिनके मलयालम और कश्मीरी साहित्य के अनुवादों को अंतरराष्ट्रीय मान्यता मिली है।<br>• इस पुस्तक की कहानियाँ <b>उन्माद, इच्छा, जाति तथा केरल के रोज़मर्रा के जीवन</b> से संबंधित हैं और अपरंपरागत कथन शैली में प्रस्तुत हैं।<br>• यह पुस्तक मलयालम से अनुवाद है, संस्कृत कविता से नहीं, तथा यह कथा साहित्य है, इतिहास या राजनीतिक निबंधों का संग्रह नहीं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि पुस्तक सांस्कृतिक अंतर्दृष्टि युक्त प्रशंसित मलयालम कृति है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000073521","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Preamble","question":{"en":"Which document is known as the 'Identity Card' of the Indian Constitution? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कौन-सा दस्तावेज़ भारतीय संविधान का 'पहचान पत्र' कहलाता है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The Preamble","hi":"प्रस्तावना"},"2":{"en":"The Directive Principles of State Policy","hi":"राज्य के नीति निर्देशक तत्व"},"3":{"en":"The Seventh Schedule","hi":"सातवीं अनुसूची"},"4":{"en":"The Fundamental Rights","hi":"मूल अधिकार"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – The Preamble</b><br>The <b>Preamble</b> is called the <b>'identity card' of the Constitution</b>, because it presents the source of authority, the nature of the state and the objectives of the Constitution in a nutshell.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Preamble declares India to be a <b>sovereign, socialist, secular, democratic republic</b> securing justice, liberty, equality and fraternity.<br>• It was amended once, by the <b>42nd Amendment Act, 1976</b>, which added the words 'socialist', 'secular' and 'integrity'.<br>• The Preamble is <b>not enforceable in a court of law</b>, but it is used as an aid to interpretation and is part of the Constitution, as held in the <b>Kesavananda Bharati case</b>.<br>• The words 'We, the People of India' show that <b>sovereignty lies with the people</b>.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because the Preamble is known as the identity card of the Constitution.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – प्रस्तावना</b><br><b>प्रस्तावना</b> को <b>संविधान का 'पहचान पत्र'</b> कहा जाता है, क्योंकि वह संक्षेप में सत्ता के स्रोत, राज्य की प्रकृति तथा संविधान के उद्देश्यों को प्रस्तुत करती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• प्रस्तावना भारत को <b>संप्रभु, समाजवादी, धर्मनिरपेक्ष, लोकतांत्रिक गणराज्य</b> घोषित करती है, जो न्याय, स्वतंत्रता, समता तथा बंधुत्व सुनिश्चित करता है।<br>• इसमें एक बार, <b>42वें संशोधन अधिनियम, 1976</b> द्वारा संशोधन हुआ, जिसने 'समाजवादी', 'धर्मनिरपेक्ष' तथा 'अखंडता' शब्द जोड़े।<br>• प्रस्तावना <b>न्यायालय में प्रवर्तनीय नहीं</b> है, परंतु इसका उपयोग व्याख्या के सहायक रूप में होता है और यह संविधान का भाग है, जैसा <b>केशवानंद भारती मामले</b> में अभिनिर्धारित हुआ।<br>• 'हम भारत के लोग' शब्द दर्शाते हैं कि <b>संप्रभुता जनता में निहित है</b>।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि प्रस्तावना को संविधान का पहचान पत्र कहा जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000073522","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Local Government","question":{"en":"Under which Article of the Indian Constitution is the Metropolitan Planning Committee provided? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान के किस अनुच्छेद में महानगरपालिका योजना समिति (Metropolitan Planning Committee) का प्रावधान है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Article 243ZD","hi":"अनुच्छेद 243ZD"},"2":{"en":"Article 243ZE","hi":"अनुच्छेद 243ZE"},"3":{"en":"Article 243ZF","hi":"अनुच्छेद 243ZF"},"4":{"en":"Article 243ZG","hi":"अनुच्छेद 243ZG"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Article 243ZE</b><br><b>Article 243ZE</b>, inserted by the <b>74th Constitutional Amendment Act, 1992</b>, provides for the constitution of a <b>Metropolitan Planning Committee</b> in every metropolitan area with a population of ten lakh or more, to prepare a draft development plan.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Article 243ZD</b> provides for District Planning Committees, and <b>243ZF</b> deals with the continuance of existing laws, while <b>243ZG</b> bars courts from interfering in electoral matters of municipalities.<br>• Two-thirds of the members of the Metropolitan Planning Committee are elected by the elected members of the municipalities and chairpersons of panchayats in the metropolitan area.<br>• The 74th Amendment (Part IXA) added Articles <b>243P to 243ZG</b> and the <b>Twelfth Schedule</b> with 18 municipal functions.<br>• A metropolitan area is one with a population of <b>ten lakh or more</b>, as notified by the Governor.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because the Metropolitan Planning Committee is provided under Article 243ZE.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – अनुच्छेद 243ZE</b><br><b>74वें संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम, 1992</b> से जोड़ा गया <b>अनुच्छेद 243ZE</b> दस लाख या अधिक जनसंख्या वाले प्रत्येक महानगर क्षेत्र में विकास योजना का प्रारूप तैयार करने हेतु <b>महानगरपालिका योजना समिति</b> के गठन का प्रावधान करता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 243ZD</b> जिला योजना समितियों का, <b>243ZF</b> विद्यमान विधियों के चालू रहने का तथा <b>243ZG</b> नगरपालिकाओं के निर्वाचन विषयों में न्यायालयों के हस्तक्षेप के वर्जन का प्रावधान करता है।<br>• महानगरपालिका योजना समिति के दो-तिहाई सदस्य महानगर क्षेत्र की नगरपालिकाओं के निर्वाचित सदस्यों तथा पंचायतों के अध्यक्षों द्वारा निर्वाचित होते हैं।<br>• 74वें संशोधन (भाग IXA) ने <b>अनुच्छेद 243P से 243ZG</b> तथा 18 नगरपालिका कार्यों वाली <b>बारहवीं अनुसूची</b> जोड़ी।<br>• महानगर क्षेत्र वह है जिसकी जनसंख्या <b>दस लाख या अधिक</b> हो, जैसा राज्यपाल अधिसूचित करे।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि महानगरपालिका योजना समिति का प्रावधान अनुच्छेद 243ZE में है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000073523","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Local Government","question":{"en":"What is the primary objective of the Metropolitan Planning Committee under Article 243ZE of the Indian Constitution? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान के अनुच्छेद 243ZE के अंतर्गत महानगरपालिका योजना समिति का प्रमुख उद्देश्य क्या है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To collect taxes from the metropolitan residents","hi":"महानगर निवासियों से कर वसूल करना"},"2":{"en":"To prepare a draft development plan for the metro area","hi":"महानगर क्षेत्र के लिए विकास योजना का प्रारूप तैयार करना"},"3":{"en":"To manage the police force within the metropolitan limits","hi":"महानगर सीमा के भीतर पुलिस बल का प्रबंधन करना"},"4":{"en":"To adjudicate disputes between different Municipalities","hi":"विभिन्न नगरपालिकाओं के बीच विवादों का निर्णय करना"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – To prepare a draft development plan for the metro area</b><br>The primary objective of the <b>Metropolitan Planning Committee</b> under <b>Article 243ZE</b> is to <b>prepare a draft development plan</b> for the metropolitan area as a whole, covering shared resources, infrastructure and environmental conservation.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Committee's functions include <b>matters of common interest between municipalities and panchayats, coordinated spatial planning, sharing of water and other resources and integrated infrastructure development</b>.<br>• Metropolitan planning is advisory and recommendatory; implementation rests with the municipalities and state government.<br>• Taxation, policing and adjudication of disputes are functions of municipalities, states and courts respectively, not of the Committee.<br>• The 74th Amendment made such committees mandatory in metropolitan areas to avoid fragmented planning across multiple municipal bodies.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because the Committee prepares a draft development plan for the metropolitan area.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – महानगर क्षेत्र के लिए विकास योजना का प्रारूप तैयार करना</b><br><b>अनुच्छेद 243ZE</b> के अंतर्गत <b>महानगरपालिका योजना समिति</b> का प्रमुख उद्देश्य समग्र महानगर क्षेत्र के लिए <b>विकास योजना का प्रारूप तैयार करना</b> है, जिसमें साझा संसाधन, अवसंरचना तथा पर्यावरण संरक्षण सम्मिलित हों।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• समिति के कार्यों में <b>नगरपालिकाओं तथा पंचायतों के बीच साझा हित के विषय, समन्वित स्थानिक नियोजन, जल एवं अन्य संसाधनों की साझेदारी तथा एकीकृत अवसंरचना विकास</b> सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• महानगर नियोजन सलाहकारी एवं संस्तुतिकारी है; क्रियान्वयन नगरपालिकाओं तथा राज्य सरकार के पास रहता है।<br>• कराधान, पुलिसिंग तथा विवादों का निर्णय क्रमशः नगरपालिकाओं, राज्यों एवं न्यायालयों के कार्य हैं, समिति के नहीं।<br>• 74वें संशोधन ने अनेक नगरपालिका निकायों में खंडित नियोजन से बचने हेतु महानगर क्षेत्रों में ऐसी समितियाँ अनिवार्य कीं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि समिति महानगर क्षेत्र की विकास योजना का प्रारूप तैयार करती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000073524","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Agriculture","question":{"en":"Which of the following crops is commonly cultivated in both northern and southern states during the Kharif season? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी फसल खरीफ मौसम में उत्तर तथा दक्षिण दोनों राज्यों में सामान्यतः उगाई जाती है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Wheat","hi":"गेहूँ"},"2":{"en":"Barley","hi":"जौ"},"3":{"en":"Rice","hi":"चावल"},"4":{"en":"Mustard","hi":"सरसों"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Rice</b><br><b>Rice</b> is the principal <b>kharif</b> crop and is grown in both northern and southern states, from West Bengal, Uttar Pradesh and Punjab to Tamil Nadu, Andhra Pradesh and Kerala.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Rice requires <b>high temperature (above 25°C), high humidity and 100-200 cm of rainfall</b>, and is grown in irrigated and rainfed lowlands.<br>• India is the <b>second-largest producer of rice</b> in the world after China and the largest exporter.<br>• <b>Wheat, barley and mustard</b> are rabi crops sown in winter, so they are not kharif crops.<br>• Rice-growing areas include the <b>Ganga-Brahmaputra plains, coastal plains, deltas of the east coast and the terraced valleys of the Himalayas</b>.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because rice is commonly grown in both north and south India in the kharif season.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – चावल</b><br><b>चावल</b> प्रमुख <b>खरीफ</b> फसल है और उत्तर तथा दक्षिण दोनों राज्यों में उगाया जाता है – पश्चिम बंगाल, उत्तर प्रदेश एवं पंजाब से लेकर तमिलनाडु, आंध्र प्रदेश तथा केरल तक।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• चावल के लिए <b>उच्च तापमान (25°C से अधिक), उच्च आर्द्रता तथा 100-200 सेमी वर्षा</b> आवश्यक है, और यह सिंचित एवं वर्षा-आधारित निचली भूमि में उगाया जाता है।<br>• भारत विश्व में चीन के बाद <b>दूसरा सबसे बड़ा चावल उत्पादक</b> तथा सबसे बड़ा निर्यातक है।<br>• <b>गेहूँ, जौ तथा सरसों</b> रबी की फसलें हैं जो शीतकाल में बोई जाती हैं, इसलिए वे खरीफ फसलें नहीं हैं।<br>• चावल उत्पादक क्षेत्रों में <b>गंगा-ब्रह्मपुत्र मैदान, तटीय मैदान, पूर्वी तट के डेल्टा तथा हिमालय की सीढ़ीनुमा घाटियाँ</b> सम्मिलित हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि खरीफ मौसम में चावल उत्तर तथा दक्षिण भारत दोनों में उगाया जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000073525","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Minerals","question":{"en":"Which location of Karnataka is associated with manganese mining? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कर्नाटक का कौन-सा स्थान मैंगनीज़ खनन से संबंधित है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Tumakuru","hi":"तुमकुरु"},"2":{"en":"Bhandara","hi":"भंडारा"},"3":{"en":"Kalahandi","hi":"कालाहांडी"},"4":{"en":"Vijayapura","hi":"विजयपुरा"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Tumakuru</b><br><b>Tumakuru</b> district in Karnataka is associated with <b>manganese mining</b>, and Karnataka is one of India's leading producers of manganese ore along with Madhya Pradesh, Maharashtra and Odisha.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Karnataka's mineral belt includes manganese and iron ore in <b>Ballari (Sandur), Chitradurga, Tumakuru, Uttara Kannada and Shivamogga</b> districts.<br>• <b>Bhandara</b> is in Maharashtra and <b>Kalahandi</b> in Odisha, both with manganese deposits, but they are not in Karnataka.<br>• Manganese is used mainly in <b>steel making, dry-cell batteries and ferro-alloys</b>, and India is a significant producer of manganese ore.<br>• <b>Vijayapura</b> in Karnataka is known for limestone and has no major manganese mining.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because Tumakuru in Karnataka is associated with manganese mining.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – तुमकुरु</b><br>कर्नाटक का <b>तुमकुरु</b> जिला <b>मैंगनीज़ खनन</b> से संबंधित है, और कर्नाटक मध्य प्रदेश, महाराष्ट्र तथा ओडिशा के साथ भारत के प्रमुख मैंगनीज़ अयस्क उत्पादक राज्यों में है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• कर्नाटक की खनिज पट्टी में <b>बल्लारी (संदूर), चित्रदुर्ग, तुमकुरु, उत्तर कन्नड़ तथा शिवमोग्गा</b> जिलों में मैंगनीज़ एवं लोह अयस्क हैं।<br>• <b>भंडारा</b> महाराष्ट्र में तथा <b>कालाहांडी</b> ओडिशा में है, दोनों में मैंगनीज़ भंडार हैं, परंतु वे कर्नाटक में नहीं हैं।<br>• मैंगनीज़ मुख्यतः <b>इस्पात निर्माण, शुष्क सेल बैटरी तथा फेरो-मिश्रातुओं</b> में प्रयुक्त होता है, और भारत मैंगनीज़ अयस्क का महत्वपूर्ण उत्पादक है।<br>• कर्नाटक का <b>विजयपुरा</b> चूना-पत्थर के लिए जाना जाता है और वहाँ बड़ा मैंगनीज़ खनन नहीं है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि कर्नाटक का तुमकुरु मैंगनीज़ खनन से संबंधित है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000073526","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Preamble","question":{"en":"What does the concept of “Republic” in the Preamble to the Indian Constitution imply? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान की प्रस्तावना में \"गणराज्य\" (Republic) की अवधारणा क्या दर्शाती है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"States possess sovereignty","hi":"राज्यों में संप्रभुता निहित है"},"2":{"en":"India has a written Constitution","hi":"भारत का लिखित संविधान है"},"3":{"en":"Head of State is elected","hi":"राज्य का प्रधान निर्वाचित होता है"},"4":{"en":"Judiciary is independent","hi":"न्यायपालिका स्वतंत्र है"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Head of State is elected</b><br>The word <b>'Republic'</b> in the Preamble implies that the <b>Head of State (the President) is elected</b> by the people's representatives for a fixed term, and that no office is hereditary.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• In a republic, <b>public offices are open to all citizens</b> and political authority derives from the people, not from birth or divine right.<br>• India is a <b>parliamentary</b> republic, so the real executive is the Council of Ministers responsible to Parliament.<br>• A <b>written Constitution</b> and an <b>independent judiciary</b> are features of the Indian Constitution but not the meaning of the word republic.<br>• Sovereignty in India is vested in the people, not in the states, which is why India is described as a <b>sovereign, democratic republic</b>.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because a republic means the Head of State is elected.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – राज्य का प्रधान निर्वाचित होता है</b><br>प्रस्तावना में <b>'गणराज्य'</b> शब्द का अर्थ है कि <b>राज्य का प्रधान (राष्ट्रपति) जनप्रतिनिधियों द्वारा निश्चित अवधि के लिए निर्वाचित</b> होता है और कोई पद वंशानुगत नहीं है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• गणराज्य में <b>लोक पद सभी नागरिकों के लिए खुले</b> होते हैं और राजनीतिक सत्ता जनता से प्राप्त होती है, जन्म या दैवी अधिकार से नहीं।<br>• भारत <b>संसदीय</b> गणराज्य है, इसलिए वास्तविक कार्यपालिका मंत्रिपरिषद है जो संसद के प्रति उत्तरदायी है।<br>• <b>लिखित संविधान</b> तथा <b>स्वतंत्र न्यायपालिका</b> भारतीय संविधान की विशेषताएँ हैं, परंतु गणराज्य शब्द का अर्थ नहीं।<br>• भारत में संप्रभुता जनता में निहित है, राज्यों में नहीं, इसीलिए भारत को <b>संप्रभु, लोकतांत्रिक गणराज्य</b> कहा जाता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि गणराज्य का अर्थ है राज्य का प्रधान निर्वाचित होना।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000073527","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"A private citizen witnesses a police officer struggling to prevent the escape of an accused who has been lawfully arrested in connection with a robbery offence. The police officer reasonably requests the citizen’s assistance, but the citizen refuses. Which of the following statements is most accurate under the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक निजी नागरिक देखता है कि एक पुलिस अधिकारी लूट के अपराध में विधिवत गिरफ्तार अभियुक्त के भागने को रोकने के लिए संघर्ष कर रहा है। पुलिस अधिकारी उचित रूप से नागरिक से सहायता का अनुरोध करता है, परंतु नागरिक मना कर देता है। भारतीय न्याय संहिता, 2023 के अंतर्गत निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा कथन सर्वाधिक सटीक है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The citizen has complete discretion whether to assist.","hi":"नागरिक को पूर्ण विवेकाधिकार है कि सहायता करे या नहीं।"},"2":{"en":"Assistance is mandatory only for government servants.","hi":"सहायता केवल सरकारी कर्मचारियों के लिए अनिवार्य है।"},"3":{"en":"Duty to assist in preventing escape of arrested person when reasonably required.","hi":"जब उचित रूप से अपेक्षित हो तो गिरफ्तार व्यक्ति के पलायन को रोकने में सहायता करने का कर्तव्य है।"},"4":{"en":"Assistance becomes mandatory only after written orders from a magistrate.","hi":"सहायता मजिस्ट्रेट के लिखित आदेश के बाद ही अनिवार्य होती है।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Duty to assist in preventing escape of arrested person when reasonably required.</b><br>Under the <b>Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023</b>, every person is bound to <b>assist a public servant reasonably demanding help</b> in preventing the escape of an arrested person or in apprehending an offender, and refusing such assistance is an offence.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The duty to assist applies to <b>every person</b>, not only government servants, and arises when the demand is <b>reasonable</b> and the person is present and able to help.<br>• Refusal to assist a public servant when bound to do so is punishable with simple imprisonment up to three months, a fine up to ₹2,500 or both.<br>• Similar duties include assisting in the <b>prevention of offences against public tranquillity</b> and in <b>apprehending a proclaimed offender</b>.<br>• No written order of a magistrate is needed, and the citizen does not have complete discretion, so options (1), (2) and (4) are wrong.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because there is a duty to assist when reasonably required.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – जब उचित रूप से अपेक्षित हो तो गिरफ्तार व्यक्ति के पलायन को रोकने में सहायता करने का कर्तव्य है।</b><br><b>भारतीय न्याय संहिता, 2023</b> के अंतर्गत प्रत्येक व्यक्ति <b>लोक सेवक की उचित रूप से की गई सहायता की माँग</b> पूरी करने के लिए बाध्य है, जब गिरफ्तार व्यक्ति के पलायन को रोकने या अपराधी को पकड़ने की बात हो, और ऐसी सहायता से इनकार करना अपराध है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सहायता का कर्तव्य <b>प्रत्येक व्यक्ति</b> पर लागू होता है, केवल सरकारी कर्मचारियों पर नहीं, और यह तब उत्पन्न होता है जब माँग <b>उचित</b> हो तथा व्यक्ति उपस्थित एवं सहायता करने में समर्थ हो।<br>• जब सहायता करना बाध्यकारी हो और लोक सेवक की सहायता से इनकार किया जाए तो तीन माह तक साधारण कारावास, ₹2,500 तक जुर्माना या दोनों हो सकते हैं।<br>• समान कर्तव्यों में <b>लोक शांति के विरुद्ध अपराधों को रोकने</b> तथा <b>घोषित अपराधी को पकड़ने</b> में सहायता सम्मिलित है।<br>• मजिस्ट्रेट के लिखित आदेश की आवश्यकता नहीं है, और नागरिक को पूर्ण विवेकाधिकार नहीं है, इसलिए विकल्प (1), (2) तथा (4) गलत हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि उचित रूप से अपेक्षित होने पर सहायता करने का कर्तव्य है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000073528","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"In the context of economic reforms since 1991, which form of privatisation involves transferring ownership of public enterprises entirely to the private sector? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"1991 के बाद के आर्थिक सुधारों के संदर्भ में, निजीकरण का कौन-सा रूप सार्वजनिक उद्यमों का स्वामित्व पूर्णतः निजी क्षेत्र को हस्तांतरित करता है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Cooperative ownership","hi":"सहकारी स्वामित्व"},"2":{"en":"Joint sector partnership","hi":"संयुक्त क्षेत्र साझेदारी"},"3":{"en":"Total denationalisation","hi":"पूर्ण विनिजीकरण (Total denationalisation)"},"4":{"en":"Partial disinvestment","hi":"आंशिक विनिवेश"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Total denationalisation</b><br><b>Total denationalisation</b> is the form of privatisation in which the <b>entire ownership of a public enterprise is transferred to the private sector</b>, unlike partial disinvestment where the government retains a stake.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Partial disinvestment</b> means selling only a part of the government's equity, keeping control or a substantial share.<br>• <b>Joint sector</b> partnership involves both government and private ownership, and <b>cooperative ownership</b> transfers ownership to a cooperative of workers or users.<br>• Examples of total privatisation include the sale of <b>Air India to the Tata Group in 2021</b> and strategic disinvestment of other PSUs.<br>• The New Public Sector Enterprise Policy of 2021 keeps only strategic sectors with a bare minimum presence of government-owned enterprises.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because total denationalisation transfers ownership entirely to the private sector.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – पूर्ण विनिजीकरण (Total denationalisation)</b><br><b>पूर्ण विनिजीकरण</b> निजीकरण का वह रूप है जिसमें <b>सार्वजनिक उद्यम का संपूर्ण स्वामित्व निजी क्षेत्र को हस्तांतरित</b> हो जाता है, जबकि आंशिक विनिवेश में सरकार की हिस्सेदारी बनी रहती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>आंशिक विनिवेश</b> का अर्थ है सरकारी इक्विटी का केवल एक भाग बेचना, जिसमें नियंत्रण या पर्याप्त हिस्सा सरकार के पास रहता है।<br>• <b>संयुक्त क्षेत्र</b> साझेदारी में सरकार तथा निजी दोनों का स्वामित्व होता है, और <b>सहकारी स्वामित्व</b> में स्वामित्व श्रमिकों या उपयोगकर्ताओं की सहकारी समिति को जाता है।<br>• पूर्ण निजीकरण के उदाहरणों में <b>2021 में एयर इंडिया का टाटा समूह को विक्रय</b> तथा अन्य सार्वजनिक उद्यमों का रणनीतिक विनिवेश सम्मिलित है।<br>• 2021 की नई सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र उद्यम नीति केवल रणनीतिक क्षेत्रों में सरकारी उद्यमों की न्यूनतम उपस्थिति रखती है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि पूर्ण विनिजीकरण स्वामित्व पूर्णतः निजी क्षेत्र को हस्तांतरित करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000073529","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Motion","question":{"en":"A body is projected vertically upward with an initial speed of 20 m/s (meters per second). Neglecting air resistance and taking g (gravity) = 10<sup>m/s<sup>2</sup></sup> (meters per second squared), what maximum height does it reach above the point of projection? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक पिंड को 20 मीटर/सेकंड की प्रारंभिक चाल से ऊर्ध्वाधर ऊपर की ओर फेंका जाता है। वायु प्रतिरोध की उपेक्षा करते हुए तथा g = 10 मीटर/सेकंड² लेते हुए, यह प्रक्षेपण बिंदु से कितनी अधिकतम ऊँचाई तक पहुँचेगा? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"10 (meter)","hi":"10 मीटर"},"2":{"en":"15 (meter)","hi":"15 मीटर"},"3":{"en":"20 (meter)","hi":"20 मीटर"},"4":{"en":"25 (meter)","hi":"25 मीटर"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 20 (meter)</b><br>Using \\(v^2 = u^2 - 2gh\\) with final velocity \\(v = 0\\) at the highest point, \\(h = \\frac{u^2}{2g} = \\frac{20 \\times 20}{2 \\times 10}\\) = <b>20 m</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• At the highest point the velocity becomes <b>zero</b>, but the acceleration remains \\(g\\) downwards throughout the motion.<br>• The total time of flight is \\(\\frac{2u}{g}\\) = 4 seconds, and the time to reach the top is \\(\\frac{u}{g}\\) = 2 seconds.<br>• The motion is uniformly accelerated with \\(a = -g\\) during the upward journey and \\(a = +g\\) during the fall.<br>• Maximum height is proportional to the <b>square of the initial speed</b>, so doubling the speed makes the height four times greater.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because the maximum height reached is 20 metres.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 20 मीटर</b><br>\\(v^2 = u^2 - 2gh\\) का उपयोग करते हुए, जहाँ उच्चतम बिंदु पर अंतिम वेग \\(v = 0\\) है, \\(h = \\frac{u^2}{2g} = \\frac{20 \\times 20}{2 \\times 10}\\) = <b>20 मीटर</b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• उच्चतम बिंदु पर वेग <b>शून्य</b> हो जाता है, परंतु त्वरण पूरी गति में नीचे की ओर \\(g\\) ही रहता है।<br>• कुल उड़ान समय \\(\\frac{2u}{g}\\) = 4 सेकंड है, और शीर्ष तक पहुँचने का समय \\(\\frac{u}{g}\\) = 2 सेकंड।<br>• ऊपर जाते समय गति \\(a = -g\\) तथा गिरते समय \\(a = +g\\) के साथ एकसमान त्वरित होती है।<br>• अधिकतम ऊँचाई <b>प्रारंभिक चाल के वर्ग</b> के समानुपाती होती है, इसलिए चाल दोगुनी करने पर ऊँचाई चार गुनी हो जाती है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि प्राप्त अधिकतम ऊँचाई 20 मीटर है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000073530","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Indian National Congress","question":{"en":"At which session was the Purna Swaraj resolution formally adopted? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"पूर्ण स्वराज का प्रस्ताव औपचारिक रूप से किस अधिवेशन में अपनाया गया? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Lahore","hi":"लाहौर"},"2":{"en":"Karachi","hi":"कराची"},"3":{"en":"Lucknow","hi":"लखनऊ"},"4":{"en":"Surat","hi":"सूरत"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Lahore</b><br>The <b>Purna Swaraj</b> resolution was formally adopted at the <b>Lahore session of the Indian National Congress</b> in <b>December 1929</b>, under the presidency of <b>Jawaharlal Nehru</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Congress declared <b>complete independence</b> as its goal and fixed <b>26 January 1930</b> as the first Independence Day, which is why Republic Day is celebrated on that date.<br>• The Lahore session also authorised the launch of a <b>civil disobedience movement</b>, which began with the Dandi March in 1930.<br>• The <b>Karachi session (1931)</b> adopted the Fundamental Rights and Economic Policy resolution, and the <b>Lucknow session (1916)</b> saw the Congress-League pact.<br>• The <b>Surat session (1907)</b> witnessed the split between moderates and extremists.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because Purna Swaraj was adopted at the Lahore session.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – लाहौर</b><br><b>पूर्ण स्वराज</b> का प्रस्ताव <b>दिसंबर 1929</b> में <b>भारतीय राष्ट्रीय कांग्रेस के लाहौर अधिवेशन</b> में, <b>जवाहरलाल नेहरू</b> की अध्यक्षता में औपचारिक रूप से अपनाया गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• कांग्रेस ने <b>पूर्ण स्वतंत्रता</b> को अपना लक्ष्य घोषित किया और <b>26 जनवरी 1930</b> को प्रथम स्वतंत्रता दिवस तय किया, इसी कारण उस तिथि पर गणतंत्र दिवस मनाया जाता है।<br>• लाहौर अधिवेशन ने <b>सविनय अवज्ञा आंदोलन</b> के आरंभ का अधिकार भी दिया, जो 1930 में दांडी मार्च से प्रारंभ हुआ।<br>• <b>कराची अधिवेशन (1931)</b> ने मूल अधिकार तथा आर्थिक नीति प्रस्ताव अपनाया, और <b>लखनऊ अधिवेशन (1916)</b> में कांग्रेस-लीग समझौता हुआ।<br>• <b>सूरत अधिवेशन (1907)</b> में उदारवादियों तथा उग्रवादियों में विभाजन हुआ।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि पूर्ण स्वराज लाहौर अधिवेशन में अपनाया गया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000073531","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"The curved surface area of a hemisphere is 2772 cm². Find its volume. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक अर्धगोले का वक्र पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल 2772 cm² है। उसका आयतन ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"19404 cm³"},"2":{"en":"29404 cm³"},"3":{"en":"20404 cm³"},"4":{"en":"12304 cm³"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Curved surface area of a hemisphere \\(= 2\\pi r^2 = 2772\\)<br>\\(2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times r^2 = 2772 \\Rightarrow r^2 = \\frac{2772 \\times 7}{44} = 441\\)<br>\\(r = 21\\) cm<br>Volume \\(= \\frac{2}{3}\\pi r^3 = \\frac{2}{3} \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 9261 = \\boxed{19404}\\) cm³<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 19404 cm³.</b>","hi":"अर्धगोले का वक्र पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल \\(= 2\\pi r^2 = 2772\\)<br>\\(2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times r^2 = 2772 \\Rightarrow r^2 = \\frac{2772 \\times 7}{44} = 441\\)<br>\\(r = 21\\) cm<br>आयतन \\(= \\frac{2}{3}\\pi r^3 = \\frac{2}{3} \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 9261 = \\boxed{19404}\\) cm³<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 19404 cm³ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000073532","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"The space diagonal of a cube of side 3 cm is: [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"3 cm भुजा वाले घन का अंतरिक्ष विकर्ण है: [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5.19 cm"},"2":{"en":"4.32 cm"},"3":{"en":"3.46 cm"},"4":{"en":"6.90 cm"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Space diagonal of a cube \\(= \\sqrt{3}a\\)<br>\\(= \\sqrt{3} \\times 3 = 3\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(= 3 \\times 1.732 = \\boxed{5.19}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 5.19 cm.</b>","hi":"घन का अंतरिक्ष विकर्ण \\(= \\sqrt{3}a\\)<br>\\(= \\sqrt{3} \\times 3 = 3\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(= 3 \\times 1.732 = \\boxed{5.19}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 5.19 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000073533","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"The area of an equilateral triangle is 16√3 cm². What is its side length? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक समबाहु त्रिभुज का क्षेत्रफल 16√3 cm² है। उसकी भुजा की लंबाई क्या है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8 cm"},"2":{"en":"18 cm"},"3":{"en":"12 cm"},"4":{"en":"9 cm"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Area \\(= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}a^2 = 16\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(a^2 = 64 \\Rightarrow a = \\boxed{8}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 8 cm.</b>","hi":"क्षेत्रफल \\(= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}a^2 = 16\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(a^2 = 64 \\Rightarrow a = \\boxed{8}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 8 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000073534","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"What is the value of x if (2x − y)² = 25 and y = 5? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि (2x − y)² = 25 और y = 5 है, तो x का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5"},"2":{"en":"10"},"3":{"en":"25"},"4":{"en":"15"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Put \\(y = 5\\): \\((2x - 5)^2 = 25\\)<br>Taking the positive root, \\(2x - 5 = 5 \\Rightarrow 2x = 10\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{5}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 5.</b>","hi":"\\(y = 5\\) रखिए: \\((2x - 5)^2 = 25\\)<br>धनात्मक मूल लेने पर, \\(2x - 5 = 5 \\Rightarrow 2x = 10\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{5}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 5 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000073535","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"Calculate the volume of a cylinder whose base area is 1386 cm² and height is 50 cm. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"उस बेलन का आयतन ज्ञात कीजिए जिसका आधार क्षेत्रफल 1386 cm² और ऊँचाई 50 cm है। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"56800 cm³"},"2":{"en":"56589 cm³"},"3":{"en":"35648 cm³"},"4":{"en":"69300 cm³"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Volume of a cylinder = base area × height<br>\\(= 1386 \\times 50 = \\boxed{69300}\\) cm³<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 69300 cm³.</b>","hi":"बेलन का आयतन = आधार क्षेत्रफल × ऊँचाई<br>\\(= 1386 \\times 50 = \\boxed{69300}\\) cm³<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 69300 cm³ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000073536","section":"MATH","topic":"Time Speed and Distance","question":{"en":"A boy goes to school at 3 km/hr and returns at a speed of 2 km/hr. If he takes 5 hours in all, find the distance from his village to school. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक लड़का 3 km/घंटा की चाल से स्कूल जाता है और 2 km/घंटा की चाल से वापस आता है। यदि उसे कुल 5 घंटे लगते हैं, तो उसके गाँव से स्कूल की दूरी ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4 km"},"2":{"en":"6 km"},"3":{"en":"8 km"},"4":{"en":"10 km"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Let the distance be \\(d\\) km<br>\\(\\frac{d}{3} + \\frac{d}{2} = 5\\)<br>\\(\\frac{5d}{6} = 5 \\Rightarrow d = \\boxed{6}\\) km<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 6 km.</b>","hi":"दूरी \\(d\\) km मानिए<br>\\(\\frac{d}{3} + \\frac{d}{2} = 5\\)<br>\\(\\frac{5d}{6} = 5 \\Rightarrow d = \\boxed{6}\\) km<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 6 km है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000073537","section":"MATH","topic":"Time Speed and Distance","question":{"en":"A person travels a fixed distance at a certain usual speed. If he reduces his speed by 6 km/h, he reaches his destination 20 minutes late. If he reduces his speed by 2 km/h, he reaches 5 minutes late. Find his usual speed. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक व्यक्ति एक निश्चित दूरी अपनी सामान्य चाल से तय करता है। यदि वह अपनी चाल 6 km/घंटा कम कर दे, तो वह 20 मिनट देरी से पहुँचता है। यदि वह चाल 2 km/घंटा कम कर दे, तो वह 5 मिनट देरी से पहुँचता है। उसकी सामान्य चाल ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12 km/h","hi":"12 km/घंटा"},"2":{"en":"18 km/h","hi":"18 km/घंटा"},"3":{"en":"24 km/h","hi":"24 km/घंटा"},"4":{"en":"30 km/h","hi":"30 km/घंटा"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Let usual speed be \\(v\\) and distance \\(d\\)<br>\\(\\frac{d}{v-6} - \\frac{d}{v} = \\frac{20}{60} = \\frac{1}{3} \\Rightarrow \\frac{6d}{v(v-6)} = \\frac{1}{3} \\Rightarrow d = \\frac{v(v-6)}{18}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{d}{v-2} - \\frac{d}{v} = \\frac{5}{60} = \\frac{1}{12} \\Rightarrow \\frac{2d}{v(v-2)} = \\frac{1}{12} \\Rightarrow d = \\frac{v(v-2)}{24}\\)<br>Equating: \\(24(v - 6) = 18(v - 2) \\Rightarrow 6v = 108\\)<br>\\(v = \\boxed{18}\\) km/h<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 18 km/h.</b>","hi":"सामान्य चाल \\(v\\) और दूरी \\(d\\) मानिए<br>\\(\\frac{d}{v-6} - \\frac{d}{v} = \\frac{20}{60} = \\frac{1}{3} \\Rightarrow \\frac{6d}{v(v-6)} = \\frac{1}{3} \\Rightarrow d = \\frac{v(v-6)}{18}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{d}{v-2} - \\frac{d}{v} = \\frac{5}{60} = \\frac{1}{12} \\Rightarrow \\frac{2d}{v(v-2)} = \\frac{1}{12} \\Rightarrow d = \\frac{v(v-2)}{24}\\)<br>बराबर करने पर: \\(24(v - 6) = 18(v - 2) \\Rightarrow 6v = 108\\)<br>\\(v = \\boxed{18}\\) km/घंटा<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 18 km/घंटा है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000073538","section":"MATH","topic":"Number System","question":{"en":"If √6ⁿ = 216, then the value of n is: [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि √6ⁿ = 216 है, तो n का मान है: [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"9"},"2":{"en":"6"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(6^{n/2} = 216 = 6^3\\)<br>\\(\\frac{n}{2} = 3 \\Rightarrow n = \\boxed{6}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 6.</b>","hi":"\\(6^{n/2} = 216 = 6^3\\)<br>\\(\\frac{n}{2} = 3 \\Rightarrow n = \\boxed{6}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 6 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000073539","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Find the value of \\(\\frac{(0.02)^3-(0.002)^3}{0.0004+0.00004+0.000004}\\). [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"\\(\\frac{(0.02)^3-(0.002)^3}{0.0004+0.00004+0.000004}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0.015"},"2":{"en":"0.025"},"3":{"en":"0.018"},"4":{"en":"0.035"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Use \\(a^3 - b^3 = (a - b)(a^2 + ab + b^2)\\) with \\(a = 0.02\\), \\(b = 0.002\\)<br>Here \\(a^2 + ab + b^2 = 0.0004 + 0.00004 + 0.000004\\), which cancels with the denominator<br>Value \\(= a - b = 0.02 - 0.002 = \\boxed{0.018}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 0.018.</b>","hi":"\\(a^3 - b^3 = (a - b)(a^2 + ab + b^2)\\) का प्रयोग कीजिए, जहाँ \\(a = 0.02\\), \\(b = 0.002\\)<br>यहाँ \\(a^2 + ab + b^2 = 0.0004 + 0.00004 + 0.000004\\), जो हर से कट जाता है<br>मान \\(= a - b = 0.02 - 0.002 = \\boxed{0.018}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 0.018 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000073540","section":"MATH","topic":"Number System","question":{"en":"How many pairs of (x, y) are possible such that the number 763x4y2 is divisible by 9? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"(x, y) के कितने युग्म संभव हैं जिनके लिए संख्या 763x4y2, 9 से विभाज्य हो? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"15 pairs","hi":"15 युग्म"},"2":{"en":"18 pairs","hi":"18 युग्म"},"3":{"en":"12 pairs","hi":"12 युग्म"},"4":{"en":"11 pairs","hi":"11 युग्म"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Sum of digits \\(= 7 + 6 + 3 + x + 4 + y + 2 = 22 + x + y\\)<br>For divisibility by 9: \\(x + y = 5\\) or \\(x + y = 14\\)<br>\\(x + y = 5\\): 6 pairs; \\(x + y = 14\\): 5 pairs<br>Total \\(= \\boxed{11}\\) pairs<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 11 pairs.</b>","hi":"अंकों का योग \\(= 7 + 6 + 3 + x + 4 + y + 2 = 22 + x + y\\)<br>9 से विभाज्यता के लिए: \\(x + y = 5\\) या \\(x + y = 14\\)<br>\\(x + y = 5\\): 6 युग्म; \\(x + y = 14\\): 5 युग्म<br>कुल \\(= \\boxed{11}\\) युग्म<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 11 युग्म है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000073541","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In ΔXYZ, the medians intersect at centroid G. If the total length of the median starting from vertex Z is 9 cm, what is the length of segment GZ? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"ΔXYZ में, माध्यिकाएँ केन्द्रक G पर मिलती हैं। यदि शीर्ष Z से शुरू होने वाली माध्यिका की कुल लंबाई 9 cm है, तो खंड GZ की लंबाई क्या है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2 cm"},"2":{"en":"9 cm"},"3":{"en":"6 cm"},"4":{"en":"3 cm"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The centroid divides each median in the ratio 2 : 1 from the vertex<br>\\(GZ = \\frac{2}{3} \\times 9 = \\boxed{6}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 6 cm.</b>","hi":"केन्द्रक प्रत्येक माध्यिका को शीर्ष से 2 : 1 के अनुपात में विभाजित करता है<br>\\(GZ = \\frac{2}{3} \\times 9 = \\boxed{6}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 6 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000073542","section":"MATH","topic":"Number System","question":{"en":"What is the sum of all prime numbers between 20 and 35? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"20 और 35 के बीच की सभी अभाज्य संख्याओं का योग क्या है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"74"},"2":{"en":"83"},"3":{"en":"92"},"4":{"en":"65"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Primes between 20 and 35: 23, 29, 31<br>Sum \\(= 23 + 29 + 31 = \\boxed{83}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 83.</b>","hi":"20 और 35 के बीच अभाज्य संख्याएँ: 23, 29, 31<br>योग \\(= 23 + 29 + 31 = \\boxed{83}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 83 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000073543","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"A and B can complete a work in 20 days and 60 days respectively. A starts and they work alternately. Find the total number of days required. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"A और B एक कार्य को क्रमशः 20 दिन और 60 दिन में पूरा कर सकते हैं। A प्रारंभ करता है और वे बारी-बारी से कार्य करते हैं। आवश्यक कुल दिनों की संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"15 days","hi":"15 दिन"},"2":{"en":"10 days","hi":"10 दिन"},"3":{"en":"20 days","hi":"20 दिन"},"4":{"en":"30 days","hi":"30 दिन"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Work in 2 days (A then B) \\(= \\frac{1}{20} + \\frac{1}{60} = \\frac{4}{60} = \\frac{1}{15}\\)<br>So 15 such pairs of days are needed<br>Total days \\(= 15 \\times 2 = \\boxed{30}\\) days<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 30 days.</b>","hi":"2 दिनों में कार्य (A फिर B) \\(= \\frac{1}{20} + \\frac{1}{60} = \\frac{4}{60} = \\frac{1}{15}\\)<br>अतः ऐसे 15 जोड़े दिन चाहिए<br>कुल दिन \\(= 15 \\times 2 = \\boxed{30}\\) दिन<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 30 दिन है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000073544","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If cosec A + cot A = 7, find the value of tan A. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि cosec A + cot A = 7 है, तो tan A का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{24}{7}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{5}{12}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{7}{24}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{12}{5}\\)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\csc A + \\cot A = \\frac{1 + \\cos A}{\\sin A} = \\cot\\frac{A}{2} = 7\\)<br>So \\(\\tan\\frac{A}{2} = \\frac{1}{7}\\)<br>\\(\\tan A = \\frac{2\\tan(A/2)}{1 - \\tan^2(A/2)} = \\frac{2/7}{1 - 1/49} = \\frac{2/7}{48/49}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{7}{24}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): \\(\\frac{7}{24}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(\\csc A + \\cot A = \\frac{1 + \\cos A}{\\sin A} = \\cot\\frac{A}{2} = 7\\)<br>अतः \\(\\tan\\frac{A}{2} = \\frac{1}{7}\\)<br>\\(\\tan A = \\frac{2\\tan(A/2)}{1 - \\tan^2(A/2)} = \\frac{2/7}{1 - 1/49} = \\frac{2/7}{48/49}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{7}{24}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): \\(\\frac{7}{24}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000073545","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(x = 10 + 3\\sqrt{11}\\), what is the value of \\(\\left(\\sqrt{x} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\right)^2\\)? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(x = 10 + 3\\sqrt{11}\\) है, तो \\(\\left(\\sqrt{x} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\right)^2\\) का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12"},"2":{"en":"14"},"3":{"en":"16"},"4":{"en":"18"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{x} = \\frac{1}{10 + 3\\sqrt{11}} = \\frac{10 - 3\\sqrt{11}}{100 - 99} = 10 - 3\\sqrt{11}\\)<br>\\(x + \\frac{1}{x} = (10 + 3\\sqrt{11}) + (10 - 3\\sqrt{11}) = 20\\)<br>\\(\\left(\\sqrt{x} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\right)^2 = x + \\frac{1}{x} - 2 = 20 - 2\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{18}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 18.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{1}{x} = \\frac{1}{10 + 3\\sqrt{11}} = \\frac{10 - 3\\sqrt{11}}{100 - 99} = 10 - 3\\sqrt{11}\\)<br>\\(x + \\frac{1}{x} = (10 + 3\\sqrt{11}) + (10 - 3\\sqrt{11}) = 20\\)<br>\\(\\left(\\sqrt{x} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\right)^2 = x + \\frac{1}{x} - 2 = 20 - 2\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{18}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 18 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000073546","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Two equal parallel chords of a circle lie on opposite sides of the centre. The perpendicular distance between the chords is 6 cm. If the radius of the circle is 5 cm, find the length of each chord (in cm). [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक वृत्त की दो समान समांतर जीवाएँ केंद्र के विपरीत ओर स्थित हैं। जीवाओं के बीच लंबवत दूरी 6 cm है। यदि वृत्त की त्रिज्या 5 cm है, तो प्रत्येक जीवा की लंबाई (cm में) ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2 cm"},"2":{"en":"4 cm"},"3":{"en":"6 cm"},"4":{"en":"8 cm"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Equal chords are equidistant from the centre, so each is \\(\\frac{6}{2} = 3\\) cm from O<br>Half chord \\(= \\sqrt{5^2 - 3^2} = \\sqrt{16} = 4\\) cm<br>Chord \\(= 2 \\times 4 = \\boxed{8}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 8 cm.</b>","hi":"समान जीवाएँ केंद्र से समान दूरी पर होती हैं, अतः प्रत्येक केंद्र O से \\(\\frac{6}{2} = 3\\) cm दूर है<br>आधी जीवा \\(= \\sqrt{5^2 - 3^2} = \\sqrt{16} = 4\\) cm<br>जीवा \\(= 2 \\times 4 = \\boxed{8}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 8 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000073547","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"A tangent AB is drawn to a circle at point A. If the radius OA = 4 cm and ∠AOB = 60°, find the length of the tangent AB. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक वृत्त पर बिंदु A से स्पर्श रेखा AB खींची गई है। यदि त्रिज्या OA = 4 cm और ∠AOB = 60° है, तो स्पर्श रेखा AB की लंबाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4√3 cm"},"2":{"en":"4 cm"},"3":{"en":"2 cm"},"4":{"en":"2√3 cm"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"A tangent is perpendicular to the radius at the point of contact, so ∠OAB = 90°<br>In right ΔOAB, \\(\\tan 60^\\circ = \\frac{AB}{OA}\\)<br>\\(AB = 4\\sqrt{3} = \\boxed{4\\sqrt{3}}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 4√3 cm.</b>","hi":"स्पर्श रेखा स्पर्श बिंदु पर त्रिज्या के लंबवत होती है, अतः ∠OAB = 90°<br>समकोण ΔOAB में, \\(\\tan 60^\\circ = \\frac{AB}{OA}\\)<br>\\(AB = 4\\sqrt{3} = \\boxed{4\\sqrt{3}}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 4√3 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000073548","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A hemispherical bowl of internal radius r is filled with water. A solid sphere of radius r/2 is gently placed into the bowl. If the water overflows, what fraction of the bowl's total volume overflows? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"आंतरिक त्रिज्या r वाला एक अर्धगोलाकार कटोरा जल से भरा है। त्रिज्या r/2 वाला एक ठोस गोला धीरे से कटोरे में रखा जाता है। यदि जल बह जाता है, तो कटोरे के कुल आयतन का कितना भाग बहता है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{4}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{8}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{6}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Volume of the bowl \\(= \\frac{2}{3}\\pi r^3\\)<br>Volume of the sphere \\(= \\frac{4}{3}\\pi\\left(\\frac{r}{2}\\right)^3 = \\frac{\\pi r^3}{6}\\)<br>Overflow fraction \\(= \\frac{\\pi r^3/6}{2\\pi r^3/3} = \\frac{1}{6} \\times \\frac{3}{2} = \\boxed{\\frac{1}{4}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\).</b>","hi":"कटोरे का आयतन \\(= \\frac{2}{3}\\pi r^3\\)<br>गोले का आयतन \\(= \\frac{4}{3}\\pi\\left(\\frac{r}{2}\\right)^3 = \\frac{\\pi r^3}{6}\\)<br>बहने वाला भाग \\(= \\frac{\\pi r^3/6}{2\\pi r^3/3} = \\frac{1}{6} \\times \\frac{3}{2} = \\boxed{\\frac{1}{4}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000073549","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"A clock shows 4:20. What is the angle in radians between the hour hand and the minute hand? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक घड़ी में 4:20 बजे हैं। घंटे की सुई और मिनट की सुई के बीच रेडियन में कोण क्या है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{\\pi}{18}\\) radians","hi":"\\(\\frac{\\pi}{18}\\) रेडियन"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{\\pi}{9}\\) radians","hi":"\\(\\frac{\\pi}{9}\\) रेडियन"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\) radians","hi":"\\(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\) रेडियन"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{\\pi}{16}\\) radians","hi":"\\(\\frac{\\pi}{16}\\) रेडियन"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Minute hand: \\(20 \\times 6^\\circ = 120^\\circ\\)<br>Hour hand: \\(4 \\times 30^\\circ + 20 \\times 0.5^\\circ = 130^\\circ\\)<br>Difference \\(= 10^\\circ = 10 \\times \\frac{\\pi}{180}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{\\pi}{18}}\\) radians<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(\\frac{\\pi}{18}\\) radians.</b>","hi":"मिनट की सुई: \\(20 \\times 6^\\circ = 120^\\circ\\)<br>घंटे की सुई: \\(4 \\times 30^\\circ + 20 \\times 0.5^\\circ = 130^\\circ\\)<br>अंतर \\(= 10^\\circ = 10 \\times \\frac{\\pi}{180}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{\\pi}{18}}\\) रेडियन<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(\\frac{\\pi}{18}\\) रेडियन है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000073550","section":"MATH","topic":"Pipe and Cistern","question":{"en":"An inlet pipe is attached to an empty tank which can fill the tank in exactly 1 hour at the rate of 2 cm/sec. The inlet pipe has a cross section of square shape with side 4 cm. An outlet pipe with a circular cross section is also attached to the tank and it can empty the tank at the rate of 7 cm/sec. When both these pipes function simultaneously, the tank gets exactly filled after 3 hrs 12 mins. Find the radius of the cross-section of the outlet pipe. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक खाली टैंक से जुड़ा एक प्रवेश पाइप उस टैंक को 2 cm/सेकंड की दर से ठीक 1 घंटे में भर सकता है। प्रवेश पाइप का अनुप्रस्थ काट 4 cm भुजा वाला वर्गाकार है। टैंक से एक वृत्तीय अनुप्रस्थ काट वाला निकास पाइप भी जुड़ा है जो 7 cm/सेकंड की दर से टैंक को खाली कर सकता है। जब दोनों पाइप एक साथ कार्य करते हैं, तो टैंक ठीक 3 घंटे 12 मिनट में भर जाता है। निकास पाइप के अनुप्रस्थ काट की त्रिज्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3 cm"},"2":{"en":"2.5 cm"},"3":{"en":"1.5 cm"},"4":{"en":"1 cm"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Inlet rate \\(= 16 \\times 2 = 32\\) cm³/s, so tank capacity \\(= 32 \\times 3600 = 115200\\) cm³<br>Time with both pipes \\(= 3\\) hr \\(12\\) min \\(= 11520\\) s<br>Net rate \\(= \\frac{115200}{11520} = 10\\) cm³/s<br>Outlet rate \\(= 32 - 10 = 22\\) cm³/s, i.e. \\(7 \\times \\pi r^2 = 22\\)<br>\\(\\pi r^2 = \\frac{22}{7} \\Rightarrow r^2 = 1 \\Rightarrow r = \\boxed{1}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 1 cm.</b>","hi":"प्रवेश दर \\(= 16 \\times 2 = 32\\) cm³/सेकंड, अतः टैंक की क्षमता \\(= 32 \\times 3600 = 115200\\) cm³<br>दोनों पाइपों के साथ समय \\(= 3\\) घंटे \\(12\\) मिनट \\(= 11520\\) सेकंड<br>शुद्ध दर \\(= \\frac{115200}{11520} = 10\\) cm³/सेकंड<br>निकास दर \\(= 32 - 10 = 22\\) cm³/सेकंड, अर्थात् \\(7 \\times \\pi r^2 = 22\\)<br>\\(\\pi r^2 = \\frac{22}{7} \\Rightarrow r^2 = 1 \\Rightarrow r = \\boxed{1}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 1 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000073551","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"In a right triangle ABC with ∠B = 90°, sin A = ? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"समकोण त्रिभुज ABC में, जहाँ ∠B = 90° है, sin A = ? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"tan C"},"2":{"en":"sin C"},"3":{"en":"cos C"},"4":{"en":"sec C"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sin A = \\frac{BC}{AC}\\) and \\(\\cos C = \\frac{BC}{AC}\\)<br>Hence \\(\\sin A = \\boxed{\\cos C}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): cos C.</b>","hi":"\\(\\sin A = \\frac{BC}{AC}\\) और \\(\\cos C = \\frac{BC}{AC}\\)<br>अतः \\(\\sin A = \\boxed{\\cos C}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): cos C है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000073552","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"Using an algebraic identity, find the value of \\(\\frac{105 \\times 105 - 95 \\times 95}{10}\\). [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"बीजगणितीय सर्वसमिका का प्रयोग करते हुए \\(\\frac{105 \\times 105 - 95 \\times 95}{10}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2"},"2":{"en":"20"},"3":{"en":"200"},"4":{"en":"2000"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(105^2 - 95^2 = (105 + 95)(105 - 95) = 200 \\times 10\\)<br>Value \\(= \\frac{2000}{10} = \\boxed{200}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 200.</b>","hi":"\\(105^2 - 95^2 = (105 + 95)(105 - 95) = 200 \\times 10\\)<br>मान \\(= \\frac{2000}{10} = \\boxed{200}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 200 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000073553","section":"MATH","topic":"Time Speed and Distance","question":{"en":"A commuter locomotive travels the initial one-third of its route at a uniform rate of 60 km/h, completing the remaining two-thirds at 90 km/h. Determine the average speed sustained over the entire trip. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक यात्री रेल इंजन अपने मार्ग का पहला एक-तिहाई भाग 60 km/घंटा की एकसमान चाल से तय करता है और शेष दो-तिहाई भाग 90 km/घंटा की चाल से पूरा करता है। पूरी यात्रा की औसत चाल ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"75 km/h","hi":"75 km/घंटा"},"2":{"en":"72 km/h","hi":"72 km/घंटा"},"3":{"en":"70 km/h","hi":"70 km/घंटा"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{540}{7}\\) km/h","hi":"\\(\\frac{540}{7}\\) km/घंटा"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Let the total distance be \\(3d\\)<br>Time \\(= \\frac{d}{60} + \\frac{2d}{90} = d\\left(\\frac{3 + 4}{180}\\right) = \\frac{7d}{180}\\)<br>Average speed \\(= \\frac{3d}{7d/180} = \\frac{540}{7}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{540}{7}}\\) km/h<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): \\(\\frac{540}{7}\\) km/h.</b>","hi":"कुल दूरी \\(3d\\) मानिए<br>समय \\(= \\frac{d}{60} + \\frac{2d}{90} = d\\left(\\frac{3 + 4}{180}\\right) = \\frac{7d}{180}\\)<br>औसत चाल \\(= \\frac{3d}{7d/180} = \\frac{540}{7}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{540}{7}}\\) km/घंटा<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): \\(\\frac{540}{7}\\) km/घंटा है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000073554","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"From a point on level ground, the angle of elevation of the top of Tower A is greater than that of Tower B. If Tower A is known to be farther from the observer than Tower B, then which statement must be true? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"समतल भूमि पर एक बिंदु से, मीनार A के शिखर का उन्नयन कोण मीनार B के उन्नयन कोण से अधिक है। यदि मीनार A प्रेक्षक से मीनार B की तुलना में अधिक दूर है, तो कौन-सा कथन अनिवार्यतः सत्य है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Tower A is taller than Tower B.","hi":"मीनार A, मीनार B से ऊँची है।"},"2":{"en":"Tower B is taller than Tower A.","hi":"मीनार B, मीनार A से ऊँची है।"},"3":{"en":"Both towers have equal heights.","hi":"दोनों मीनारों की ऊँचाई समान है।"},"4":{"en":"No conclusion can be drawn without knowing exact distances.","hi":"सटीक दूरियाँ जाने बिना कोई निष्कर्ष नहीं निकाला जा सकता।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Height \\(= \\) distance \\(\\times \\tan(\\text{angle of elevation})\\)<br>For A both the distance and \\(\\tan\\theta\\) are greater than for B<br>So \\(h_A = d_A\\tan\\theta_A > d_B\\tan\\theta_B = h_B\\)<br>Hence \\(\\boxed{\\text{Tower A is taller than Tower B}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Tower A is taller than Tower B..</b>","hi":"ऊँचाई \\(= \\) दूरी \\(\\times \\tan(\\text{उन्नयन कोण})\\)<br>A के लिए दूरी और \\(\\tan\\theta\\) दोनों B से अधिक हैं<br>अतः \\(h_A = d_A\\tan\\theta_A > d_B\\tan\\theta_B = h_B\\)<br>इसलिए \\(\\boxed{\\text{मीनार A, मीनार B से ऊँची है}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): मीनार A, मीनार B से ऊँची है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000073555","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Two circles have radii of 13 cm and 8 cm. If the distance between their centres is 5 cm, which of the following statements is true regarding the common tangents that can be drawn to this pair of circles? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दो वृत्तों की त्रिज्याएँ 13 cm और 8 cm हैं। यदि उनके केंद्रों के बीच की दूरी 5 cm है, तो इस वृत्त-युग्म पर खींची जा सकने वाली उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखाओं के संबंध में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा कथन सत्य है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"No common tangent can be drawn because one circle lies entirely inside the other without touching.","hi":"कोई उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा नहीं खींची जा सकती क्योंकि एक वृत्त बिना स्पर्श किए पूर्णतः दूसरे के भीतर है।"},"2":{"en":"There is exactly one common tangent because the two circles touch internally.","hi":"ठीक एक उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा है क्योंकि दोनों वृत्त आंतरिक रूप से स्पर्श करते हैं।"},"3":{"en":"There are exactly two common tangents because the two circles intersect at two distinct points.","hi":"ठीक दो उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखाएँ हैं क्योंकि दोनों वृत्त दो भिन्न बिंदुओं पर प्रतिच्छेद करते हैं।"},"4":{"en":"There are exactly three common tangents because the two circles touch each other externally.","hi":"ठीक तीन उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखाएँ हैं क्योंकि दोनों वृत्त बाह्य रूप से एक-दूसरे को स्पर्श करते हैं।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Given \\(R = 13\\), \\(r = 8\\), \\(d = 5\\)<br>\\(R - r = 13 - 8 = 5 = d\\)<br>The circles therefore touch internally, so there is exactly one common tangent (the tangent at the point of contact)<br>Hence \\(\\boxed{\\text{There is exactly one common tangent because the two circles touch internally.}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): There is exactly one common tangent because the two circles touch internally..</b>","hi":"यहाँ \\(R = 13\\), \\(r = 8\\), \\(d = 5\\)<br>\\(R - r = 13 - 8 = 5 = d\\)<br>अतः वृत्त आंतरिक रूप से स्पर्श करते हैं, इसलिए ठीक एक उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा है (स्पर्श बिंदु पर स्पर्श रेखा)<br>इसलिए \\(\\boxed{\\text{ठीक एक उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा है क्योंकि दोनों वृत्त आंतरिक रूप से स्पर्श करते हैं।}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): ठीक एक उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा है क्योंकि दोनों वृत्त आंतरिक रूप से स्पर्श करते हैं। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000073556","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>As artificial intelligence (AI) continues to redefine industries and professions, the indispensability of uniquely human skills has become increasingly pronounced. In an era where algorithms can perform routine tasks with unerring precision and speed, individuals must cultivate abilities that machines cannot easily replicate—namely critical thinking, creativity, emotional intelligence, and adaptability.<br><br>The 21st-century workforce demands more than technical literacy; it necessitates a dynamic synergy between hard skills and soft skills. Technical prowess alone, once sufficient, now risks obsolescence unless it is paired with problem-solving capacities and an innovative mind set. Employers increasingly value candidates who can not only interpret data but also infer nuanced insights, which can not only program software but also envision novel applications beyond conventional frameworks.<br><br>Moreover, resilience and the ability to unlearn and relearn swiftly are no longer optional traits but survival mechanisms. As AI accelerates change, static knowledge bases decay at an unprecedented pace. Workers who cling rigidly to out-dated competencies inevitably find themselves outpaced, while those who embrace lifelong learning carve niches even amidst automation's relentless advance.<br><br>Ultimately, it is not a competition between humans and machines, but between adaptive and static mind sets. In this fluid landscape, mastering uniquely human attributes is not merely advantageous; it is existentially imperative.<br><br><br>Identify the sentence with the correct use of the semicolon: [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The 21st-century workforce demands more than technical literacy, it necessitates a dynamic synergy between hard and soft skills."},"2":{"en":"The 21st-century workforce demands more than technical literacy; it necessitates a dynamic synergy between hard and soft skills."},"3":{"en":"The 21st-century workforce demands more than technical literacy: it necessitates a dynamic synergy between hard and soft skills."},"4":{"en":"The 21st-century workforce demands more than technical literacy; necessitating a dynamic synergy between hard and soft skills."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: A semicolon can join two closely related independent clauses.</b><br>Both “the workforce demands …” and “it necessitates …” are complete clauses.<br>Option B joins them correctly without a conjunction.<br>A is a comma splice; D leaves a fragment after the semicolon.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): The 21st-century workforce demands more than technical literacy; it necessitates a dynamic synergy between hard and soft skills..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000073557","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>As artificial intelligence (AI) continues to redefine industries and professions, the indispensability of uniquely human skills has become increasingly pronounced. In an era where algorithms can perform routine tasks with unerring precision and speed, individuals must cultivate abilities that machines cannot easily replicate—namely critical thinking, creativity, emotional intelligence, and adaptability.<br><br>The 21st-century workforce demands more than technical literacy; it necessitates a dynamic synergy between hard skills and soft skills. Technical prowess alone, once sufficient, now risks obsolescence unless it is paired with problem-solving capacities and an innovative mind set. Employers increasingly value candidates who can not only interpret data but also infer nuanced insights, which can not only program software but also envision novel applications beyond conventional frameworks.<br><br>Moreover, resilience and the ability to unlearn and relearn swiftly are no longer optional traits but survival mechanisms. As AI accelerates change, static knowledge bases decay at an unprecedented pace. Workers who cling rigidly to out-dated competencies inevitably find themselves outpaced, while those who embrace lifelong learning carve niches even amidst automation's relentless advance.<br><br>Ultimately, it is not a competition between humans and machines, but between adaptive and static mind sets. In this fluid landscape, mastering uniquely human attributes is not merely advantageous; it is existentially imperative.<br><br><br>Which choice correctly maintains parallel structure? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Individuals must cultivate critical thinking, being creative, emotional intelligence, and adapt."},"2":{"en":"Individuals must cultivate critical thinking, creativity, emotional intelligence, and adaptability."},"3":{"en":"Individuals must cultivate critically thinking, creativity, emotional intelligence, and adapt."},"4":{"en":"Individuals must cultivate critical thinking, creating, emotional intelligence, and adapting."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Items in a list should have the same grammatical form.</b><br>B uses four parallel noun phrases: critical thinking, creativity, emotional intelligence and adaptability.<br>The other options mix gerunds, adverbs and base verbs.<br>Parallel structure makes the list clear and consistent.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Individuals must cultivate critical thinking, creativity, emotional intelligence, and adaptability..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000073558","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>As artificial intelligence (AI) continues to redefine industries and professions, the indispensability of uniquely human skills has become increasingly pronounced. In an era where algorithms can perform routine tasks with unerring precision and speed, individuals must cultivate abilities that machines cannot easily replicate—namely critical thinking, creativity, emotional intelligence, and adaptability.<br><br>The 21st-century workforce demands more than technical literacy; it necessitates a dynamic synergy between hard skills and soft skills. Technical prowess alone, once sufficient, now risks obsolescence unless it is paired with problem-solving capacities and an innovative mind set. Employers increasingly value candidates who can not only interpret data but also infer nuanced insights, which can not only program software but also envision novel applications beyond conventional frameworks.<br><br>Moreover, resilience and the ability to unlearn and relearn swiftly are no longer optional traits but survival mechanisms. As AI accelerates change, static knowledge bases decay at an unprecedented pace. Workers who cling rigidly to out-dated competencies inevitably find themselves outpaced, while those who embrace lifelong learning carve niches even amidst automation's relentless advance.<br><br>Ultimately, it is not a competition between humans and machines, but between adaptive and static mind sets. In this fluid landscape, mastering uniquely human attributes is not merely advantageous; it is existentially imperative.<br><br><br>What is the closest synonym for “indispensability” as used in the passage? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Optionality"},"2":{"en":"Necessity"},"3":{"en":"Uncertainty"},"4":{"en":"Difficulty"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Indispensability (अपरिहार्यता) = the quality of being essential.</b><br>Uniquely human skills have become increasingly necessary.<br>“Necessity” is the closest synonym.<br>Optionality is the opposite; uncertainty and difficulty do not fit.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Necessity.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000073559","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>As artificial intelligence (AI) continues to redefine industries and professions, the indispensability of uniquely human skills has become increasingly pronounced. In an era where algorithms can perform routine tasks with unerring precision and speed, individuals must cultivate abilities that machines cannot easily replicate—namely critical thinking, creativity, emotional intelligence, and adaptability.<br><br>The 21st-century workforce demands more than technical literacy; it necessitates a dynamic synergy between hard skills and soft skills. Technical prowess alone, once sufficient, now risks obsolescence unless it is paired with problem-solving capacities and an innovative mind set. Employers increasingly value candidates who can not only interpret data but also infer nuanced insights, which can not only program software but also envision novel applications beyond conventional frameworks.<br><br>Moreover, resilience and the ability to unlearn and relearn swiftly are no longer optional traits but survival mechanisms. As AI accelerates change, static knowledge bases decay at an unprecedented pace. Workers who cling rigidly to out-dated competencies inevitably find themselves outpaced, while those who embrace lifelong learning carve niches even amidst automation's relentless advance.<br><br>Ultimately, it is not a competition between humans and machines, but between adaptive and static mind sets. In this fluid landscape, mastering uniquely human attributes is not merely advantageous; it is existentially imperative.<br><br><br>What is the meaning of “static” in the phrase “static knowledge bases decay”? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Constant and unchanging"},"2":{"en":"Rapidly growing"},"3":{"en":"Highly dynamic"},"4":{"en":"Specialized and complex"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Static (स्थिर) = fixed or unchanging.</b><br>Static knowledge fails to evolve and therefore becomes obsolete rapidly.<br>Rapid growth and dynamism are opposite qualities.<br>Specialization and complexity do not define “static.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Constant and unchanging.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000073560","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>As artificial intelligence (AI) continues to redefine industries and professions, the indispensability of uniquely human skills has become increasingly pronounced. In an era where algorithms can perform routine tasks with unerring precision and speed, individuals must cultivate abilities that machines cannot easily replicate—namely critical thinking, creativity, emotional intelligence, and adaptability.<br><br>The 21st-century workforce demands more than technical literacy; it necessitates a dynamic synergy between hard skills and soft skills. Technical prowess alone, once sufficient, now risks obsolescence unless it is paired with problem-solving capacities and an innovative mind set. Employers increasingly value candidates who can not only interpret data but also infer nuanced insights, which can not only program software but also envision novel applications beyond conventional frameworks.<br><br>Moreover, resilience and the ability to unlearn and relearn swiftly are no longer optional traits but survival mechanisms. As AI accelerates change, static knowledge bases decay at an unprecedented pace. Workers who cling rigidly to out-dated competencies inevitably find themselves outpaced, while those who embrace lifelong learning carve niches even amidst automation's relentless advance.<br><br>Ultimately, it is not a competition between humans and machines, but between adaptive and static mind sets. In this fluid landscape, mastering uniquely human attributes is not merely advantageous; it is existentially imperative.<br><br><br>According to the passage, why is lifelong learning crucial in the age of AI? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Because machines can be easily programmed to adapt emotions."},"2":{"en":"Because human knowledge remains unchanged over decades."},"3":{"en":"Because static knowledge becomes obsolete quickly and adaptability ensures relevance."},"4":{"en":"Because creativity is no longer valued in technical fields."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: Static knowledge decays quickly, while learning helps workers remain relevant.</b><br>Adaptability and the capacity to unlearn and relearn are survival mechanisms.<br>The passage values creativity and rejects unchanging knowledge.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Because static knowledge becomes obsolete quickly and adaptability ensures relevance..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000073561","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the correctly spelt word.<br>The treaty marked a ___ moment in international diplomacy. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"watershed"},"2":{"en":"wotershed"},"3":{"en":"watershead"},"4":{"en":"wottershed"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Watershed (महत्वपूर्ण मोड़) = a turning point.</b><br>The correct spelling is “watershed.”<br><b>Wotershed</b> replaces “a” with “o.”<br><b>Watershead</b> and <b>wottershed</b> alter the ending or vowel.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): watershed.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000073562","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the appropriate preposition.<br>The event transpired ___ circumstances still unknown to the public. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"under"},"2":{"en":"amidst"},"3":{"en":"within"},"4":{"en":"inside"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Collocation: “Under circumstances” means in particular conditions.</b><br>The event occurred under circumstances unknown to the public.<br>“Amidst” means surrounded by, while “within” and “inside” indicate containment.<br>Only “under” fits the established phrase.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): amidst.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000073563","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br>Following the geopolitical crisis triggered by the Russia-Ukraine war,<br>P. compelling European nations to accelerate their transition towards renewable energy<br>Q. while industries struggled to maintain production levels amid skyrocketing operational costs,<br>R. forcing governments to implement emergency measures such as energy rationing,<br>S. severe disruptions in energy supplies sent natural gas prices soaring, [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"PRSQ"},"2":{"en":"SRPQ"},"3":{"en":"QSPR"},"4":{"en":"SRPQ"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: SRPQ</b><br>S states the supply disruption and soaring gas prices.<br>R gives the emergency government response.<br>P adds the renewable-energy transition, and Q concludes with industrial costs.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): SRPQ.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000073564","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with appropriate parts of speech.<br>The committee's decision was met with widespread ___ among the academic community, although some dissenters voiced their reservations. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"acclaimed"},"2":{"en":"acclaiming"},"3":{"en":"acclimated"},"4":{"en":"acclaim"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Acclaim (प्रशंसा) = public praise.</b><br>The adjective “widespread” and preposition “with” require the noun “acclaim.”<br>“Acclaimed” is a verb or adjective, and “acclaiming” a participle.<br>“Acclimated” means adapted.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): acclaim.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000073565","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Identify the error in the sentence.<br>I bought <b>the</b> pair of shoes from the online store. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"store"},"2":{"en":"the"},"3":{"en":"online"},"4":{"en":"shoes"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Use “a pair of shoes” for a nonspecific purchase.</b><br>Correct sentence: “I bought <b>a</b> pair of shoes from the online store.”<br>“The” would require a pair already identified in context.<br>The erroneous word is “the.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): the.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000073566","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br>The legacy of colonialism<br>P. contributing to persistent economic and social inequalities<br>Q. as former colonies navigate issues of national identity and sovereignty<br>R. continues to shape global political dynamics,<br>S. while striving for reparations and historical accountability [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"SRPQ"},"2":{"en":"QPSR"},"3":{"en":"PQRS"},"4":{"en":"RPQS"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: RPQS</b><br>R supplies the main predicate: colonialism continues to shape politics.<br>P states its contribution to persistent inequalities.<br>Q and S describe former colonies’ identity struggles and pursuit of accountability.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): RPQS.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000073567","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"What does the idiom “Get up on the wrong side of the bed” mean? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To start the day in a bad mood"},"2":{"en":"To wake up very early in the morning"},"3":{"en":"To feel refreshed after a good night's sleep"},"4":{"en":"To accidentally fall out of bed"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Get up on the wrong side of the bed (दिन की शुरुआत खराब मूड से करना) = be irritable.</b><br>Example: “He is unusually grumpy; he must have got up on the wrong side of the bed.”<br>The idiom does not refer to literal waking or falling.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): To start the day in a bad mood.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000073568","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct idiom for the word highlighted in bold.<br>“The president told the people that if they wanted the country to continue to move forward, they should reelect him. He said that to elect his opponent would be like <b>changing horses in midstream</b>.” [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Switching to a new leader or plan in the middle of an ongoing process"},"2":{"en":"Going horseback riding during a flood"},"3":{"en":"Trying a new hobby while still learning the old one"},"4":{"en":"Giving up on something before even starting it"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Change horses in midstream = change leaders or plans midway.</b><br>The president warns against replacing leadership during an ongoing national effort.<br>The phrase is figurative, not literal riding.<br>It concerns untimely transition, not abandoning a task.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Switching to a new leader or plan in the middle of an ongoing process.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000073569","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Which of the given options arranges the following sentences in the most logical sequence to form a meaningful paragraph?<br>1. Social stratification refers to the hierarchical arrangement of individuals in a society based on factors such as wealth, power and prestige.<br>2. This stratification system shapes individuals' access to resources and opportunities in society.<br>3. Sociologists have identified various forms of social stratification, including caste, class and race.<br>4. Social mobility, the ability to move between different strata, varies across societies and can be influenced by education and employment opportunities.<br>5. The study of social stratification is crucial in understanding inequality and its impact on individuals and communities. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2-3-4-1-5"},"2":{"en":"1-3-2-4-5"},"3":{"en":"2-4-5-1-3"},"4":{"en":"3-5-4-1-2"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 1-3-2-4-5</b><br>Sentence 1 defines stratification, and sentence 3 gives its forms.<br>Sentence 2 explains its effects, followed by social mobility in 4.<br>Sentence 5 concludes with the importance of studying it.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 1-3-2-4-5.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000073570","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Which of the given options arranges the following sentences in the most logical sequence to form a meaningful paragraph?<br>1. It helps safeguard individual freedoms and maintain the rule of law in the country.<br>2. The executive branch implements laws, while the legislative branch makes laws, and the judiciary interprets them.<br>3. The separation of powers is a core principle in many democratic systems, such as the United States.<br>4. The separation of powers is a model for governance in which the functions of government are divided into distinct branches.<br>5. This system prevents any one branch from gaining too much power and ensures checks and balances. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2-4-3-1-5"},"2":{"en":"1-3-2-4-5"},"3":{"en":"1-2-3-4-5"},"4":{"en":"4-5-2-3-1"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 4-5-2-3-1</b><br>Sentence 4 defines the model, and sentence 5 explains checks and balances.<br>Sentence 2 assigns the branches’ functions, followed by democratic examples in 3.<br>Sentence 1 concludes with its protection of freedom and law.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 4-5-2-3-1.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000073571","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate synonym of the given word: <b>BANTER</b> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"chitchat"},"2":{"en":"Ridicule"},"3":{"en":"Argument"},"4":{"en":"Lecture"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Banter (हँसी-मज़ाक) = light, playful conversation.</b><br><b>Chitchat (गपशप)</b> = informal conversation ✔<br><b>Ridicule (उपहास)</b> = mockery<br><b>Argument (बहस)</b> = dispute; <b>lecture (व्याख्यान)</b> = formal talk.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): chitchat.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000073572","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word. <b>Mitigate</b> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Intensify"},"2":{"en":"Reduce"},"3":{"en":"Pacify"},"4":{"en":"Ease"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Mitigate (कम करना) = reduce severity.</b><br><b>Intensify (तीव्र करना)</b> = increase in strength ✔<br><b>Reduce (घटाना)</b> = lessen<br><b>Pacify (शांत करना)</b> = calm; <b>ease (कम करना)</b> = alleviate.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Intensify.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000073573","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate synonym of the given word: <b>INSCRUTABLE</b> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mysterious"},"2":{"en":"Transparent"},"3":{"en":"Understandable"},"4":{"en":"Obvious"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Inscrutable (दुरूह) = impossible to understand.</b><br><b>Mysterious (रहस्यमय)</b> = difficult to explain ✔<br><b>Transparent (पारदर्शी)</b> = clear<br><b>Understandable (समझने योग्य)</b> = comprehensible; <b>obvious (स्पष्ट)</b> = evident.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Mysterious.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000073574","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Spot the correct spelling of a word meaning “mental picture or image”. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Imaginashun"},"2":{"en":"Imagynation"},"3":{"en":"Imagination"},"4":{"en":"Immagination"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Imagination (कल्पना) = the ability to form mental images.</b><br>The correct spelling is “imagination.”<br><b>Imaginashun</b> uses phonetic spelling; <b>imagynation</b> uses “y.”<br><b>Immagination</b> doubles “m.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Imagination.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000073575","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Choose the correct one-word substitute for: “An annual calendar containing important dates and statistical information”. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Atlas"},"2":{"en":"Chronicle"},"3":{"en":"Almanac"},"4":{"en":"Ledger"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Almanac (पंचांग) = an annual calendar with dates and data.</b><br><b>Atlas</b> = book of maps<br><b>Chronicle</b> = historical record<br><b>Ledger</b> = financial account book<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Almanac.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000073576","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Change the following from active to passive:<br>They keep the documents in this cabinet. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The documents are kept in this cabinet."},"2":{"en":"The documents were kept in this cabinet."},"3":{"en":"The documents have been kept in this cabinet."},"4":{"en":"The documents are being kept in this cabinet."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Simple present passive = am/is/are + past participle.</b><br>The plural object “documents” takes “are kept.”<br>The location phrase remains unchanged.<br>The other options change tense or aspect.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): The documents are kept in this cabinet..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000073577","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"Select the sentence containing the homonym of the highlighted word:<br>His remarks <b>struck</b> a nerve with the audience. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Lightning struck the tree during the storm."},"2":{"en":"She struck a pose on the runway."},"3":{"en":"He was struck by the depth of her words."},"4":{"en":"Workers struck over unfair wages."}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Strike = affect emotionally, hit, adopt a pose, or stop work in protest.</b><br>The original means the remarks produced a strong emotional response.<br>Option D uses “struck” for workers going on strike.<br>The other options use hitting, posing or being affected.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Workers struck over unfair wages..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000073578","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the highlighted part of the sentence:<br>She <b>is married with</b> a doctor. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"is married to"},"2":{"en":"is married of"},"3":{"en":"is marry with"},"4":{"en":"married with"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Married to someone” is the standard construction.</b><br>Correct sentence: “She <b>is married to</b> a doctor.”<br>“With” and “of” do not follow “married” in this sense.<br>The verb form “is marry” is ungrammatical.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): is married to.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000073579","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the highlighted part of the sentence:<br>I asked him <b>what was he doing there</b>. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"what he was doing there"},"2":{"en":"what he had been doing there"},"3":{"en":"what did he doing there"},"4":{"en":"what he has done there"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Embedded questions use statement word order.</b><br>Correct wording: “what <b>he was doing</b> there.”<br>The subject “he” precedes the auxiliary “was.”<br>The other options use inversion or an unsuitable tense.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): what he was doing there.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000073580","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Choose the most appropriate antonym of the underlined word.<br>The dictator was obsessed with the <b>aggrandizement</b> of his own power and wealth. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Exaltation"},"2":{"en":"Ennoblement"},"3":{"en":"Abasement"},"4":{"en":"Glorification"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Aggrandizement (विस्तार/बढ़ोतरी) = increase in power or status.</b><br><b>Exaltation (उत्कर्ष)</b> = elevation<br><b>Ennoblement (उत्कृष्ट बनाना)</b> = elevation<br><b>Abasement (अपमान/पतन)</b> = degradation ✔<br><b>Glorification (महिमामंडन)</b> = exaltation<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Abasement.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};